lculateQuotePremium` to `quotePremium`? Slightly shorter but not clearer. Keep.\n\nMaybe `mainItems` could be `nonComponentItems`? That would be more explicit. But `mainItems` is also OK. Hmm, since we renamed the function to `nonComponentBasePremium`, renaming `mainItems` to `nonComponentItems` would be consistent. Let me do that too.\n\nRefactored:\n```typescript\nconst calculateQuotePremium = (items: unknown[]): number => {\n  const nonComponentItems = items.filter((item) => !COMPONENT_TYPES.includes(itemType(item)));\n  const nonComponentBase = nonComponentItems.reduce((sum, item) => sum + nonComponentBasePremium(item), 0);\n  const runeCount = items.filter((item) => itemType(item) === \"rune\").length;\n  const policyBase = nonComponentBase + componentBasePremium(runeCount);\n  ...\n};\n```\n\nThis is clearer: non-component items → non-component base premium. Good.\n\nNow let me implement and run tests.","thinkingSignature":"reasoning_content"},{"type":"text","text":"## Refactoring Evaluation\n\n**Naming Evaluation**:\n- `itemBasePremium` → misleading: it only handles *non-component* items (amulet/sword); runes/moonstones are filtered out before it is called.\n- `(item as { type: string }).type` → repeated 3 times without naming the operation.\n- `mainItems`/`mainBase` → generic; could match the \"non-component\" concept.\n\n**Rule 1 (Tests Pass)**: All 6 passing tests currently green.\n\n**Rule 2 (Reveals Intent)**: Improve names to match actual responsibilities.\n\n**Rule 3 (No Duplication)**: Extract an `itemType` helper to remove repeated casts.\n\n**Rule 4 (Fewest Elements)**: Remove dead rune branch inside non-component pricing.\n\n---\n\n## Initial APP Mass\n\n| Component | Count | Mass |\n|-----------|-------|------|\n| Constants | 12 | 12 |\n| Bindings  | 18 | 18 |\n| Invocations | 18 | 36 |\n| Conditionals | 4 | 16 |\n| Loops | 4 | 20 |\n| Assignments | 0 | 0 |\n| **Total** | | **102** |\n\n---\n\n## Refactoring Implementation"},{"type":"toolCall","id