      | 3     | 15   |\n| Assignments      | 1     | 6    |\n| **Total Mass**   |       | **101** |\n\n**Previous (before refactor)** — `src/claim-office.ts`\n\n| Component        | Count | Mass |\n|------------------|-------|------|\n| Constants        | 15    | 15   |\n| Bindings         | 22    | 22   |\n| Invocations      | 14    | 28   |\n| Conditionals     | 3     | 12   |\n| Loops            | 3     | 15   |\n| Assignments      | 1     | 6    |\n| **Total Mass**   |       | **98** |\n\n**Mass Change**: 98 → 101 (+3)\n\n## Simple Design Rules Applied\n\n1. **Tests Pass** — verified with `pnpm test`; all 9 tests still pass.\n2. **Reveals Intent** — separated the quote calculation into `quotePremiumFor` (base-premium assembly) and `finalPremium` (policy-wide surcharge, rounding, fee). This makes the two conceptual steps explicit.\n3. **No Duplication** — no duplicated logic was present; extraction did not introduce any.\n4. **Fewest Elements** — added one helper, but it replaces an inline block that mixed responsibilities, so the net abstraction is justified by clarity.\n\n## Refactoring Applied\n\n- Extracted `finalPremium(policyBase: number): number` from `quotePremiumFor`.\n- Renamed `calculateQuotePremium` → `quotePremiumFor`.\n- Updated the call site in `processScenario`.\n\n**Tests**: All 9 passing, 24 todo."}],"details":{"mode":"single","agentScope":"both","projectAgentsDir":"/home/experimenter/experiments/runs/2026-07-24_20-30-02_claim-office-example-mapping_v6.2-with-why-cleaned-pi_kimi-k2-7-no-thinking/.pi/agents","results":[{"agent":"refactor","agentSource":"project","task":"Test file: src/claim-office.spec.ts\nImplementation file: src/claim-office.ts\nPassing tests: 9\nRecent Green phase: Generalized component pricing to handle both runes and moonstones as separate component types.\n\nRefactor the implementation while keeping all tests green.\n\nRun autonomously, return when done.","exitCode":0,"messages":[{"role":"user","content":[{"type":"text","text":"Task: Test file: src/claim-office.spec.ts\nImplementation file: src/claim-office.ts\nPassing tests: 9\nRecent Green phase: Generalized component pricing to handle both runes and moonstones as separate component types.\n\nRefactor the implementation while keeping all tests green.\n\nRun autonomously, return when done."}],"timestamp":1784925340735},{"role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"thinking","thinking":"The user is invoking the refactor subagent. I need to refactor the implementation in src/claim-office.ts while keeping all tests green. I should read the relevant files first, then evaluate naming, calculate APP mass, apply simple design rules, and document.\n\nLet me start by reading the implementation and test files.","thinkingSignature":"reasoning_content"},{"type":"toolCall","id":"functions.read:0","name":"read","arguments":{"path":"src/claim-office.ts"}},{"type":"toolCall","id":"functions.read:1","name":"read","arguments":{"path":"src/claim-office.spec.ts"}}],"api":"openai-completions","provider":"requesty","model":"tensorx/kimi-k2.7-code","usage":{"input":92,"output":101,"cacheRead":5568,"cacheWrite":0,"reasoning":63,"totalTokens":5761,"cost":{"input":0,"output":0,"cacheRead":0,"cacheWrite":0,"total":0}},"stopReason":"toolUse","timestamp":1784925340755,"responseId":"rqsty-cmpl-b64dbee8-ee52-4a63-9e00-4e2915ea0e04","responseModel":"moonshotai/kimi-k2.7-code"},{"role":"toolResult","toolCallId":"functions.read:0","toolName":"read","content":[{"type":"text","text":"const PROCESSING_FEE = 5;\nconst FIRST_INSURANCE_SURCHARGE_RATE = 0.1;\n\ntype QuoteResult = { premium: number };\ntype QuoteStep = { op: \"quote\"; items: unknown[] };\n\nconst itemType = (item: unknown): string => (item as { type: string }).type;\n\nconst nonComponentBasePremium = (item: unknown): number => {\n  const type = itemType(item);\n  if (type === \"amulet\") return 60;\n  return 100;\n};\n\nconst COMPONENT_TYPES = [\"rune\", \"moonstone\"];\nconst COMPONENT_BLOCK_SIZE = 3;\nconst COMPONENT_BLOCK_PREMIUM = 60;\nconst COMPONENT_UNIT_PREMIUM = 25;\n\nconst componentBasePremium = (count: number): number => {\n  if (count === COMPONENT_BLOCK_SIZE) return COMPONENT_BLOCK_PREMIUM;\n  return count * COMPONENT_UNIT_PREMIUM;\n};\n\nconst calculateQuotePremium = (items: unknown[]): number => {\n  const nonComponentItems = items.filter((item) => !COMPONENT_TYPES.includes(itemType(item)));\n  const nonComponentBase = nonComponentItems.reduce(\n    (sum, item) => sum + nonComponentBasePremium(item),\n    0,\n  );\n  const componentBase = COMPONENT_TYPES.reduce((sum, type) => {\n    const count = items.filter((item) => itemType(item) === type).length;\n    return sum + componentBasePremium(count);\n  }, 0);\n  const policyBase = nonComponentBase + componentBase;\n  const beforeFee = policyBase * (1 + FIRST_INSURANCE_SURCHARGE_RATE);\n  const roundedToNearestCent = Math.round(beforeFee * 100) / 100;\n  return Math.ceil(roundedToNearestCent + PROCESSING_FEE);\n};\n\nexport const processScenario = (input: { steps: unknown[] }): { results: QuoteResult[] } => {\n  const results: QuoteResult[] = [];\n  for (const step of input.steps) {\n    const quoteStep = step as QuoteStep;\n    if (quoteStep.op === \"quote\") {\n      results.push({ premium: calculateQuotePremium(quoteStep.items) });\n    }\n  }\n  return { results };\n};\n"}],"isError":false,"timestamp":1784925341525},{"role":"toolResult","toolCallId":"functions.read:1","toolName":"read","content":[{"type":"text","text":"import { describe, it, expect } from \"vitest\";\nimport { processScenario } from \"./claim-office.js\";\n\ndescribe(\"MHPCO Claim Office\", () => {\n  // Quote tests - ordered simple to complex\n  it(\"should quote an empty item list -- premium 5 G\", () => {\n    const input = {\n      customer: { yearsWithMHPCO: 0 },\n      steps: [{ op: \"quote\", items: [] }],\n    };\n    expect(processScenario(input)).toEqual({ results: [{ premium: 5 }] });\n  });\n  it(\"should quote a single sword -- premium 115 G\", () => {\n    const input = {\n      customer: { yearsWithMHPCO: 0 },\n      steps: [{ op: \"quote\", items: [{ type: \"sword\" }] }],\n    };\n    expect(processScenario(input)).toEqual({ results: [{ premium: 115 }] });\n  });\n  it(\"should quote a single amulet -- premium 71 G\", () => {\n    const input = {\n      customer: { yearsWithMHPCO: 0 },\n      steps: [{ op: \"quote\", items: [{ type: \"amulet\" }] }],\n    };\n    expect(processScenario(input)).toEqual({ results: [{ premium: 71 }] });\n  });\n  it(\"should quote a single rune -- premium 33 G\", () => {\n    const input = {\n      customer: { yearsWithMHPCO: 0 },\n      steps: [{ op: \"quote\", items: [{ type: \"rune\" }] }],\n    };\n    expect(processScenario(input)).toEqual({ results: [{ premium: 33 }] });\n  });\n  it(\"should quote two runes -- premium 60 G\", () => {\n    const input = {\n      customer: { yearsWithMHPCO: 0 },\n      steps: [{ op: \"quote\", items: [{ type: \"rune\" }, { type: \"rune\" }] }],\n    };\n    expect(processScenario(input)).toEqual({ results: [{ premium: 60 }] });\n  });\n  it(\"should quote three runes as a block -- premium 71 G\", () => {\n    const input = {\n      customer: { yearsWithMHPCO: 0 },\n      steps: [{ op: \"quote\", items: [{ type: \"rune\" }, { type: \"rune\" }, { type: \"rune\" }] }],\n    };\n    expect(processScenario(input)).toEqual({ results: [{ premium: 71 }] });\n  });\n  it(\"should quote four runes without block -- premium 115 G\", () => {\n    const input = {\n      customer: { yearsWithMHPCO: 0 },\n      steps: [\n        {\n          op: \"quote\",\n          items: [{ type: \"rune\" }, { type: \"rune\" }, { type: \"rune\" }, { type: \"rune\" }],\n        },\n      ],\n    };\n    expect(processScenario(input)).toEqual({ results: [{ premium: 115 }] });\n  });\n  it(\"should quote seven runes -- premium 198 G\", () => {\n    const input = {\n      customer: { yearsWithMHPCO: 0 },\n      steps: [\n        {\n          op: \"quote\",\n          items: [\n            { type: \"rune\" },\n            { type: \"rune\" },\n            { type: \"rune\" },\n            { type: \"rune\" },\n            { type: \"rune\" },\n            { type: \"rune\" },\n            { type: \"rune\" },\n          ],\n        },\n      ],\n    };\n    expect(processScenario(input)).toEqual({ results: [{ premium: 198 }] });\n  });\n  it(\"should quote 2 runes and 1 moonstone as different types -- premium 88 G\", () => {\n    const input = {\n      customer: { yearsWithMHPCO: 0 },\n      steps: [\n        {\n          op: \"quote\",\n          items: [{ type: \"rune\" }, { type: \"rune\" }, { type: \"moonstone\" }],\n        },\n      ],\n    };\n    expect(processScenario(input)).toEqual({ results: [{ premium: 88 }] });\n  });\n  it.todo(\"should quote 3 runes and 3 moonstones as two separate blocks -- premium 120 G\");\n  it.todo(\"should quote a cursed sword with 50% curse surcharge -- premium 155 G\");\n  it.todo(\"should quote a sword with enchantment 5 with 30% high-enchantment surcharge -- premium 135 G\");\n  it.todo(\"should quote a cursed sword with enchantment 5 with both surcharges -- premium 185 G\");\n  it.todo(\"should quote a sword for a long-standing customer (>=2 years) with 20% loyalty discount -- premium 85 G\");\n  it.todo(\"should quote a sword as first insurance with 10% surcharge -- premium 115 G\");\n  it.todo(\"should quote a second contract with 15% follow-up discount -- premium 90 G\");\n  it.todo(\"should apply item-specific modifiers per item and policy-wide modifiers to policy base -- premium 210 G\");\n  it.todo(\"should quote a newcomer with a cursed sword -- premium 165 G\");\n  it.todo(\"should quote a long-standing customer's second cursed highly-enchanted sword -- premium 160 G\");\n\n  // Claim tests\n  it.todo(\"should process a standard claim with deductible -- payout 400 G\");\n  it.todo(\"should process a claim for a rune with deductible -- payout 100 G\");\n  it.todo(\"sh