inal, so OK.\n\nSo the formula is:\n1. For each item, compute base premium (from type, with component blocks)\n2. Sum item base premiums → policy base\n3. Apply policy-wide modifiers to policy base: first insurance +10%, loyalty -20% (if years >= 2), follow-up -15% (if not first quote)\n4. Add item-specific surcharges: curse +50% of item base, enchantment >= 5 +30% of item base\n5. Add processing fee 5\n6. Round up to whole G\n\nThis is important. So `beforeFee = policyBase * policyModifierRate + sum(itemSpecificSurcharges)`. Where policyModifierRate = 1 + 0.1 (first insurance) - 0.2 (loyalty if applicable) - 0.15 (follow-up if applicable).\n\nWait, but the order might matter for rounding. The spec says intermediate amounts are kept as fractions. So we can compute exact fractional total then round at end.\n\nFor cursed sword single: policyBase = 100. policyModifierRate = 1.1 (first insurance). policyWide = 110. itemSpecific = 50. beforeFee = 160. + fee = 165. Matches.\n\nOK so I need to restructure calculateQuotePremium. Currently it does `policyBase * (1 + firstInsurance)`. I need to separate policy-wide modifiers from item-specific surcharges.\n\nFor minimal green, just add curse surcharge. I'll update quotePremiumFor to compute item-specific surcharges and add them.\n\nCurrent structure: quotePremiumFor computes policyBase, then finalPremium applies policy-wide and fee. I need to add item-specific surcharges.\n\nMinimal change: in quotePremiumFor, compute curse surcharge and add to policyBase before passing to finalPremium? No, because finalPremium applies policy-wide to policyBase. If I add curse to policyBase, then first insurance applies to curse too.\n\nWait, the formula says item-specific surcharges are added after policy-wide modifiers. But mathematically, if I have policyBase P, policy rate R, item surcharges S, then total = P*R + S + fee.\n\nSo I should pass P*R + S to finalPremium, or modify finalPremium to accept surcharges.\n\nFor minimal change, I'll 