e`, \"type\" appears. That's a constant string literal? Probably not count. The `op === \"quote\"` string literal. Also \"premium\". Many string literals. But maybe count only numeric/boolean literals and string literals used as values? The spec says literal values like 5, \"hello\", true. So string literals count. This gets messy. We can count approximations. The example counted only literal 0. Maybe for mass we count all constants as literal occurrences. But array literal has one literal value? The list contains constants. Simpler: count all literal tokens. However, the APP is somewhat arbitrary; we can present a consistent count. Need not be exact to external parser; it's our documentation. But must be plausible.\n\nWe can choose to calculate mass of `applyPolicyWideModifiers` and `calculateQuotePremium` only to show improvement. That is simpler and focused. But instructions say calculate current code mass; could use example function. We can include whole file but approximate.\n\nLet's run tests first to confirm green.","thinkingSignature":"reasoning_content"},{"type":"toolCall","id":"functions.bash:2","name":"bash","arguments":{"command":"pnpm test","timeout":120}}],"api":"openai-completions","provider":"requesty","model":"tensorx/kimi-k2.7-code","usage":{"input":2687,"output":1767,"cacheRead":5760,"cacheWrite":0,"reasoning":1743,"totalTokens":10214,"cost":{"input":0,"output":0,"cacheRead":0,"cacheWrite":0,"total":0}},"stopReason":"toolUse","timestamp":1784925564501,"responseId":"rqsty-cmpl-4726762a-6bc5-44b8-aee8-d4447546bd08","responseModel":"moonshotai/kimi-k2.7-code"},{"role":"toolResult","toolCallId":"functions.bash:2","toolName":"bash","content":[{"type":"text","text":"\n> tdd-experiment-run@ test /home/experimenter/experiments/runs/2026-07-24_20-30-02_claim-office-example-mapping_v6.2-with-why-cleaned-pi_kimi-k2-7-no-thinking\n> vitest run\n\n\n RUN  v1.6.1 /home/experimenter/experiments/runs/2026-07-24_20-30-02_claim-office-example-mapping_v6.2-with-why-