Files  1 failed (1)\n      Tests  1 failed | 19 passed | 13 todo (33)\n   Start at  20:43:35\n   Duration  164ms (transform 32ms, setup 0ms, collect 30ms, tests 9ms, environment 0ms, prepare 41ms)\n\n ELIFECYCLE  Test failed. See above for more details.\n\n\nCommand exited with code 1"}],"details":{},"isError":true,"timestamp":1784925816003},{"role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"thinking","thinking":"Red complete. Green: implement claim processing.\n\nNeed to:\n- Store policy from quote (items with properties)\n- For claim, lookup policy by index\n- Calculate insurance sum and cap\n- For each damage entry: determine reimbursement rate based on item properties, apply deductible, sum\n- Apply cap, update remaining cap\n\nFor minimal implementation, just handle the test case: sword, standard damage. \n\nI need to think about the data structure. Policy stores items array. For claim, damages array has itemType and amount. Need to find matching item in policy. For now, assume one item of each type.\n\nActually, the spec says damages array can have multiple entries of same type, and we must validate count doesn't exceed coverage. For test 20, one sword damage for one sword policy.\n\nMinimal implementation:\n- Store policies array in processScenario\n- For claim step: get policy items, compute insuranceSum, cap = 2*insuranceSum\n- Compute payout: for each damage, find item in policy, apply rules\n- For standard sword: amount - 100 deductible\n- Apply cap (not needed here), update remaining cap\n\nLet me implement.","thinkingSignature":"reasoning_content"},{"type":"text","text":"Red Phase Complete:\n**Compilation Prediction**: None expected Correct\n**Runtime Prediction**: Expected 2 results, received 1 (claim step ignored) Correct\n**Result**: Test fails as expected with assertion error\n\nProceeding to Green phase.</think>## Green -- Test 20: standard claim processing with deductible\n\n"},{"type":"toolCall","id":"functions.read:127","name":"read","arguments":{"path":"src/claim-office.ts"}}],"api":"openai-completions","provider":"requesty","model":"tensorx/kimi-k2.7-code","usage":{"input":628,"output":320,"cacheRead":67968,"cacheWrite":0,"reasoning":238,"totalTokens":68916,"cost":{"input":0,"output":0,"cacheRead":0,"cacheWrite":0,"total":0}},"stopReason":"toolUse","timestamp":1784925816006,"responseId":"rqsty-cmpl-4a460b5a-934b-46c8-91fb-d1b61010a460","responseModel":"moonshotai/kimi-k2.7-code"},{"role":"toolResult","toolCallId":"functions.read:127","toolName":"read","content":[{"type":"text","text":"const PROCESSING_FEE = 5;\nconst FIRST_INSURANCE_SURCHARGE_RATE = 0.1;\nconst CURSE_SURCHARGE_RATE = 0.5;\n\nconst COMPONENT_TYPES = [\"rune\", \"moonstone\"];\nconst COMPONENT_BLOCK_SIZE = 3;\nconst COMPONENT_BLOCK_PREMIUM = 60;\nconst COMPONENT_UNIT_PREMIUM = 25;\n\ntype QuoteResult = { premium: number };\ntype QuoteStep = { op: \"quote\"; items: unknown[] };\ntype Item = { type: string; cursed?: boolean; enchantment?: number };\ntype Customer = { yearsWithMHPCO: number };\n\nconst basePremiumForItemType = (type: string): number => (type === \"amulet\" ? 60 : 100);\n\nconst basePremiumForItem = (item: unknown): number =>\n  basePremiumForItemType((item as Item).type);\n\nconst HIGH_ENCHANTMENT_THRESHOLD = 5;\nconst HIGH_ENCHANTMENT_SURCHARGE_RATE = 0.3;\nconst LOYALTY_DISCOUNT_RATE = 0.2;\nconst LOYALTY_YEARS_THRESHOLD = 2;\nconst FOLLOW_UP_DISCOUNT_RATE = 0.15;\n\nconst surchargesForItem = (item: unknown): number => {\n  const typedItem = item as Item;\n  const basePremium = basePremiumForItem(item);\n  const curseSurcharge = typedItem.cursed ? basePremium * CURSE_SURCHARGE_RATE : 0;\n  const enchantmentSurcharge =\n    (typedItem.enchantment ?? 0) >= HIGH_ENCHANTMENT_THRESHOLD\n      ? basePremium * HIGH_ENCHANTMENT_SURCHARGE_RATE\n      : 0;\n  return curseSurcharge + enchantmentSurcharge;\n};\n\nconst componentPremiumFor = (count: number): number =>\n  count === COMPONENT_BLOCK_SIZE ? COMPONENT_BLOCK_PREMIUM : count * COMPONENT_UNIT_PREMIUM;\n\nconst calculateFinalPremium = (\n  policyBase: number,\n  itemSurcharges: number,\n  yearsWithMHPCO: number,\n  isFirstQuote: boolean,\n): number => {\n  const loyaltyDiscount =\n    yearsWithMHPCO >= LOYALTY_YEARS_THRESHOLD ? LOYALTY_DISCOUNT_RATE : 0;\n  const followUpDiscount = isFirstQuote ? 0 : FOLLOW_UP_DISCOUNT_RATE;\n  const policyMultiplier =\n    1 + FIRST_INSURANCE_SURCHARGE_RATE - loyaltyDiscount - followUpDiscount;\n  const beforeFee = policyBase * policyMultiplier + itemSurcharges;\n  const roundedToNearestCent = Math.round(beforeFee * 100) / 100;\n  return Math.ceil(roundedToNearestCent + PROCESSING_FEE);\n};\n\nconst standardItemTotals = (items: unknown[]): { base: number; surcharges: number } =>\n  items\n    .filter((item) => !COMPONENT_TYPES.includes((item as Item).type))\n    .reduce(\n      (totals, item) => ({\n        base: totals.base + basePremiumForItem(item),\n        surcharges: totals.surcharges + surchargesForItem(item),\n      }),\n      { base: 0, surcharges: 0 },\n    );\n\nconst calculateQuotePremium = (\n  items: unknown[],\n  customer: Customer,\n  isFirstQuote: boolean,\n): number => {\n  const { base: standardBase, surcharges: itemSurcharges } = standardItemTotals(items);\n  const componentBase = COMPONENT_TYPES.reduce((sum, type) => {\n    const count = items.filter((item) => (item as Item).type === type).length;\n    return sum + componentPremiumFor(count);\n  }, 0);\n  const policyBase = standardBase + componentBase;\n  return calculateFinalPremium(policyBase, itemSurcharges, customer.yearsWithMHPCO, isFirstQuote);\n};\n\ntype ScenarioInput = { customer: Customer; steps: unknown[] };\n\nexport const processScenario = (input: ScenarioInput): { results: QuoteResult[] } => {\n  const results: QuoteResult[] = [];\n  let quoteCount = 0;\n  for (const step of input.steps) {\n    const quoteStep = step as QuoteStep;\n    if (quoteStep.op === \"quote\") {\n      const isFirstQuote = quoteCount === 0;\n      results.push({\n        premium: calculateQuotePremium(quoteStep.items, input.customer, isFirstQuote),\n      });\n      quoteCount += 1;\n    }\n  }\n  return { results };\n};\n"}],"isError":false,"timestamp":1784925819827},{"role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"thinking","thinking":"I need to implement claim processing. I'll add types and helpers. Let me write a bigger update.\n\nNeed:\n- Policy type with items and remainingCap\n- Insurance value lookup\n- Claim processing\n\nMinimal for test 20:\n- Sword insurance value 1000\n- Damage: amount - 100 deductible\n- remainingCap = 2000 - 400 = 1600\n\nI'll add:\n```typescript\ntype Policy = { items: unknown[]; remainingCap: number };\n\nconst insuranceValueForItemType = (type: string): number => {\n  if (type === \"sword\") return 1000;\n  return 0;\n};\n\nconst insuranceSum = (items: unknown[]): number =>\n  items.reduce((sum, item) => sum + insuranceValueForItemType((item as Item).type), 0);\n\nconst processClaim = (policy: Policy, incident: unknown): { payout: number; remainingCap: number } => {\n  const typedIncident = incident as { damages: { itemType: string; amount: number }[] };\n  const deductible = 100;\n  let payout = 0;\n  for (const damage of typedIncident.damages) {\n    payout += damage.amount - deductible;\n  }\n  payout = Math.min(payout, policy.remainingCap);\n  return { payout: Math.floor(payout), remainingCap: policy.remainingCap - payout };\n};\n```\n\nThen processScenario needs to store policies and handle claim steps.\n\nBut processScenario currently returns QuoteResult[]. Need to change to union type.\n\nAlso, I need to track which steps are quotes to assign policy index. The `policy` field in claim refers to zero-based index of quote step in `steps` array, not result index. So I need policies array indexed by quote step order.\n\nWait, the spec says: \"later claim steps refer to a policy created by an earlier quote step via its zero-based step index in a policy field.\" So policy index is the index in the `steps` array? Or the zero-based index among quote steps?\n\n\"zero-based step index in a policy field\" - this is ambiguous. The JSON schema says \"zero-based index of the quote step that created the policy\". So it's the index of the quote step that created the policy, presumably among quote steps? Or among all steps?\n\nLooking at the schema description: \"zero-based index of the quote step that created the policy\". This suggests it's the index among quote steps. But \"step index\" could mean index in steps array.\n\nActually, in the example, steps array has quote at index 0 and claim at index 1, with policy: 0. So it works either way if there's only one quote.\n\nFor the test 16, we have two quote steps. A claim referring to policy 0 would be first quote, policy 1 would be second quote. The steps array indices would be 0 and 1 for the quotes. So both interpretations work.\n\nBut if there are non-quote steps between quotes, the interpretations differ. The spec says \"zero-based index of the quote step that created the policy\". I think it means the n-th quote step (0-based among quotes). But \"step index\" suggests index in steps array.\n\nHmm. Let me re-read: \"Steps are processed sequentially; later claim steps refer to a policy created by an earlier quote step via its zero-based step index in a policy field.\"\n\n\"step index\" = index in the steps array. So policy: 0 refers to steps[0], which must be a quote. That makes sense.\n\nSo I should index policies by steps array index. For each step, if it's a quote, store it at that index. For claim, lookup policy at input.steps[policy].\n\nBut the result array should still have one entry per step. For quote steps, result is { premium }. For claim steps, result is { payout, remainingCap }.\n\nWait, does the result array include entries for all steps in order? Yes: \"Stdout receives a JSON object with a results array of the same length and order as the input steps.\"\n\nSo I need to push a result for every step, not just quotes.\n\nLet me restructure processScenario to handle all steps. For claim steps, compute payout. For now, minimal.\n\nAlso need to handle unknown step types? Not needed.\n\nLet me update.","thinkingSignature":"reasoning_content"},{"type":"toolCall","id":"functions.edit:128","name":"edit","arguments":{"path":"src/claim-office.ts","edits":[{"oldText":"type QuoteResult = { premium: number };\ntype QuoteStep = { op: \"quote\"; items: unknown[] };\ntype Item = { type: string; cursed?: boolean; enchantment?: number };\ntype Customer = { yearsWithMHPCO: number };","newText":"type QuoteResult = { premium: number };\n type ClaimResult = { payout: number; remainingCap: number };\ntype StepResult = QuoteResult | ClaimResult;\ntype QuoteStep = { op: \"quote\"; items: unknown[] };\ntype ClaimStep = { op: \"claim\"; policy: number; incident: unknown };\ntype Item = { type: string; cursed?: boolean; enchantment?: number; material?: string };\ntype Customer = { yearsWithMHPCO: number };\ntype Policy = { items: unknown[]; remainingCap: number };"},{"oldText":"const basePremiumForItemType = (type: string): number => (type === \"amulet\" ? 60 : 100);","newText":"const basePremiumForItemType = (type: string): number => (type === \"amulet\" ? 60 : 100);\n\nconst insuranceValueForItemType = (type: string): number => {\n  if (type === \"sword\") return 1000;\n  if (type === \"amulet\") return 600;\n  if (type === \"staff\") return 800;\n  if (type === \"potion\") return 400;\n  if (type === \"rune\" || type === \"moonstone\") return 250;\n  return 0;\n};"},{"oldText":"type ScenarioInput = { customer: Customer; steps: unknown[] };\n\nexport const processScenario = (input: ScenarioInput): { results: QuoteResult[] } => {\n  const results: QuoteResult[] = [];\n  let quoteCount = 0;\n  for (const step of input.steps) {\n    const quoteStep = step as QuoteStep;\n    if (quoteStep.op === \"quote\") {\n      const isFirstQuote = quoteCount === 0;\n      results.push({\n        premium: calculateQuotePremium(quoteStep.items, input.customer, isFirstQuote),\n      });\n      quoteCount += 1;\n    }\n  }\n  return { results };\n};","newText":"type ScenarioInput = { customer: Customer; steps: unknown[] };\n\nconst DEDUCTIBLE = 100;\nconst CLAIM_CAP_MULTIPLIER = 2;\n\nconst processClaim = (policy: Policy, incident: unknown): ClaimResult => {\n  const typedIncident = incident as { damages: { itemType: string; amount: number }[] };\n  let payout = 0;\n  for (const damage of typedIncident.damages) {\n    payout += damage.amount - DEDUCTIBLE;\n  }\n  payout = Math.min(payout, policy.remainingCap);\n  return { payout: Math.floor(payout), remainingCap: policy.remainingCap - payout };\n};\n\nexport const processScenario = (input: ScenarioInput): { results: StepResult[] } => {\n  const results: StepResult[] = [];\n  const policies: (Policy | undefined)[] = [];\n  let quoteCount = 0;\n  for (const step of input.steps) {\n    const quoteStep = step as QuoteStep;\n    const claimStep = step as ClaimStep;\n    if (quoteStep.op === \"quote\") {\n      const isFirstQuote = quoteCount === 0;\n      results.push({\n        premium: calculateQuotePremium(quoteStep.items, input.customer, isFirstQuote),\n      });\n      const insuranceSum = quoteStep.items.reduce(\n        (sum, item) => sum + insuranceValueForItemType((item as Item).type),\n        0,\n      );\n      policies.push({ items: quoteStep.items, remainingCap: insuranceSum * CLAIM_CAP_MULTIPLIER });\n      quoteCount += 1;\n    } else if (claimStep.op === \"claim\") {\n      const policy = policies[claimStep.policy] as Policy;\n      const claimResult = processClaim(policy, claimStep.incident);\n      policy.remainingCap = claimResult.remainingCap;\n      results.push(claimResult);\n    }\n  }\n  return { results };\n};"}]}}],"api":"openai-completions","provider":"requesty","model":"tensorx/kimi-k2.7-code","usage":{"input":1006,"output":1899,"cacheRead":68864,"cacheWrite":0,"reasoning":889,"totalTokens":