 added to reveal intent where `unknown` casts previously obscured meaning.\n\n## Current Code Mass (Before)\n\n| Component | Count | Mass | Subtotal |\n|-----------|-------|------|----------|\n| Constants | 44 | 1 | 44 |\n| Bindings | 63 | 1 | 63 |\n| Invocations | 21 | 2 | 42 |\n| Conditionals | 13 | 4 | 52 |\n| Loops | 7 | 5 | 35 |\n| Assignments | 4 | 6 | 24 |\n| **Total** | | | **260** |\n\n## Refactorings Applied\n\n### Rule 2 — Reveal Intent\n- Introduced domain types: `Step = QuoteStep | ClaimStep`, `Incident`, `Damage`.\n- Changed internal helpers to accept `Item[]` instead of `unknown[]`, removing scattered `(item as Item)` casts.\n- Replaced the dual casts in `processScenario` with a single boundary cast to `Step`, then used discriminated-union narrowing.\n- Renamed the intermediate payout in `processClaim` to `grossPayout` to express \"before cap and floor\".\n\n### Rule 3 — No Duplication\n- Removed duplicated casting patterns (`as Item`, `as QuoteStep`, `as ClaimStep`) by leaning on the type system.\n- Replaced the `let payout` / `for...of` / `+=` mutation in `processClaim` with a single functional `reduce`.\n\n### Rule 4 — Fewest Elements\n- Removed the `else if (claimStep.op === \"claim\")` branch by relying on the discriminated union (only `QuoteStep` or `ClaimStep` are possible).\n- Removed two mutable assignments (`payout += ...`, `payout = Math.min(...)`) from `processClaim`.\n\n## New Code Mass (After)\n\n| Component | Count | Mass | Subtotal |\n|-----------|-------|------|----------|\n| Constants | 44 | 1 | 44 |\n| Bindings | 62 | 1 | 62 |\n| Invocations | 24 | 2 | 48 |\n| Conditionals | 12 | 4 | 48 |\n| Loops | 7 | 5 | 35 |\n| Assignments | 2 | 6 | 12 |\n| **Total** | | | **249** |\n\n## Refactoring Decision\n\n**Mass Change**: 260 → 249 (Δ -11)\n\nThe code is now clearer at the type level, with `Item`, `Step`, `Incident`, and `Damage` making the data flow explicit. `processClaim` no longer uses mutable state, and `processScenario` no longer casts each step to two different shapes. The slight increase in invocations (one `reduce` in `processClaim`) is offset by fewer conditionals, bindings, and assignments, and the clarity gain is significant.\n\n## Tests\n\n`pnpm test` — **20 passed, 13 todo**  \n`pnpm tsc --noEmit` — **no errors**"}],"details":{"mode":"single","agentScope":"both","projectAgentsDir":"/home/experimenter/experiments/runs/2026-07-24_20-30-02_claim-office-example-mapping_v6.2-with-why-cleaned-pi_kimi-k2-7-no-thinking/.pi/agents","results":[{"agent":"refactor","agentSource":"project","task":"Test file: src/claim-office.spec.ts\nImplementation file: src/claim-office.ts\nPassing tests: 20\nRecent Green phase: Added claim processing with deductible, cap tracking, and policy storage indexed by step.\n\nRefactor the implementation while keeping all tests green.\n\nRun autonomously, return when done.","exitCode":0,"messages":[{"role":"user","content":[{"type":"text","text":"Task: Test file: src/claim-office.spec.ts\nImplementation file: src/claim-office.ts\nPassing tests: 20\nRecent Green phase: Added claim processing with deductible, cap tracking, and policy storage indexed by step.\n\nRefactor the implementation while keeping all tests green.\n\nRun autonomously, return when done."}],"timestamp":1784925833207},{"role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"thinking","thinking":"Let me understand the task. I need to refactor the claim-office implementation while keeping all tests green. I'm operating as the refactor subagent. I need to:\n\n1. Read the implementation and test files\n2. Evaluate naming first\n3. Calculate APP mass before and after\n4. Apply Simple Design Rules in priority order\n5. Keep tests green\n6. Document decisions\n\nLet me start by reading the files.","thinkingSignature":"reasoning_content"},{"type":"text","text":"I'll refactor the implementation while keeping tests green. Let me start by examining the code and tests."},{"type":"toolCall","id":"functions.read:0","name":"read","arguments":{"path":"/home/experimenter/experiments/runs/2026-07-24_20-30-02_claim-office-example-mapping_v6.2-with-why-cleaned-pi_kimi-k2-7-no-thinking/src/claim-office.ts"}},{"type":"toolCall","id":"functions.read:1","name":"read","arguments":{"path":"/home/experimenter/experiments/runs/2026-07-24_20-30-02_claim-office-example-mapping_v6.2-with-why-cleaned-pi_kimi-k2-7-no-thinking/src/claim-office.spec.ts"}}],"api":"openai-completions","provider":"requesty","model":"tensorx/kimi-k2.7-code","usage":{"input":91,"output":235,"cacheRead":5568,"cacheWrite":0,"reasoning":86,"totalTokens":5894,"cost":{"input":0,"output":0,"cacheRead":0,"cacheWrite":0,"total":0}},"stopReason":"toolUse","timestamp":1784925833226,"responseId":"rqsty-cmpl-a9926903-675a-4d8a-8cf9-1e86dcf59440","responseModel":"moonshotai/kimi-k2.7-code"},{"role":"toolResult","toolCallId":"functions.read:0","toolName":"read","content":[{"type":"text","text":"const PROCESSING_FEE = 5;\nconst FIRST_INSURANCE_SURCHARGE_RATE = 0.1;\nconst CURSE_SURCHARGE_RATE = 0.5;\n\nconst COMPONENT_TYPES = [\"rune\", \"moonstone\"];\nconst COMPONENT_BLOCK_SIZE = 3;\nconst COMPONENT_BLOCK_PREMIUM = 60;\nconst COMPONENT_UNIT_PREMIUM = 25;\n\ntype QuoteResult = { premium: number };\n type ClaimResult = { payout: number; remainingCap: number };\ntype StepResult = QuoteResult | ClaimResult;\ntype QuoteStep = { op: \"quote\"; items: unknown[] };\ntype ClaimStep = { op: \"claim\"; policy: number; incident: unknown };\ntype Item = { type: string; cursed?: boolean; enchantment?: number; material?: string };\ntype Customer = { yearsWithMHPCO: number };\ntype Policy = { items: unknown[]; remainingCap: number };\n\nconst basePremiumForItemType = (type: string): number => (type === \"amulet\" ? 60 : 100);\n\nconst insuranceValueForItemType = (type: string): number => {\n  if (type === \"sword\") return 1000;\n  if (type === \"amulet\") return 600;\n  if (type === \"staff\") return 800;\n  if (type === \"potion\") return 400;\n  if (type === \"rune\" || type === \"moonstone\") return 250;\n  return 0;\n};\n\nconst basePremiumForItem = (item: unknown): number =>\n  basePremiumForItemType((item as Item).type);\n\nconst HIGH_ENCHANTMENT_THRESHOLD = 5;\nconst HIGH_ENCHANTMENT_SURCHARGE_RATE = 0.3;\nconst LOYALTY_DISCOUNT_RATE = 0.2;\nconst LOYALTY_YEARS_THRESHOLD = 2;\nconst FOLLOW_UP_DISCOUNT_RATE = 0.15;\n\nconst surchargesForItem = (item: unknown): number => {\n  const typedItem = item as Item;\n  const basePremium = basePremiumForItem(item);\n  const curseSurcharge = typedItem.cursed ? basePremium * CURSE_SURCHARGE_RATE : 0;\n  const enchantmentSurcharge =\n    (typedItem.enchantment ?? 0) >= HIGH_ENCHANTMENT_THRESHOLD\n      ? basePremium * HIGH_ENCHANTMENT_SURCHARGE_RATE\n      : 0;\n  return curseSurcharge + enchantmentSurcharge;\n};\n\nconst componentPremiumFor = (count: number): number =>\n  count === COMPONENT_BLOCK_SIZE ? COMPONENT_BLOCK_PREMIUM : count * COMPONENT_UNIT_PREMIUM;\n\nconst calculateFinalPremium = (\n  policyBase: number,\n  itemSurcharges: number,\n  yearsWithMHPCO: number,\n  isFirstQuote: boolean,\n): number => {\n  const loyaltyDiscount =\n    yearsWithMHPCO >= LOYALTY_YEARS_THRESHOLD ? LOYALTY_DISCOUNT_RATE : 0;\n  const followUpDiscount = isFirstQuote ? 0 : FOLLOW_UP_DISCOUNT_RATE;\n  const policyMultiplier =\n    1 + FIRST_INSURANCE_SURCHARGE_RATE - loyaltyDiscount - followUpDiscount;\n  const beforeFee = policyBase * policyMultiplier + itemSurcharges;\n  const roundedToNearestCent = Math.round(beforeFee * 100) / 100;\n  return Math.ceil(roundedToNearestCent + PROCESSING_FEE);\n};\n\nconst standardItemTotals = (items: unknown[]): { base: number; surcharges: number } =>\n  items\n    .filter((item) => !COMPONENT_TYPES.includes((item as Item).type))\n    .reduce(\n      (totals, item) => ({\n        base: totals.base + basePremiumForItem(item),\n        surcharges: totals.surcharges + surchargesForItem(item),\n      }),\n      { base: 0, surcharges: 0 },\n    );\n\nconst calculateQuotePremium = (\n  items: unknown[],\n  customer: Customer,\n  isFirstQuote: boolean,\n): number => {\n  const { base: standardBase, surcharges: itemSurcharges } = standardItemTotals(items);\n  const componentBase = COMPONENT_TYPES.reduce((sum, type) => {\n    const count = items.filter((item) => (item as Item).type === type).length;\n    return sum + componentPremiumFor(count);\n  }, 0);\n  const policyBase = standardBase + componentBase;\n  return calculateFinalPremium(policyBase, itemSurcharges, customer.yearsWithMHPCO, isFirstQuote);\n};\n\ntype ScenarioInput = { customer: Customer; steps: unknown[] };\n\nconst DEDUCTIBLE = 100;\nconst CLAIM_CAP_MULTIPLIER = 2;\n\nconst processClaim = (policy: Policy, incident: unknown): ClaimResult => {\n  const typedIncident = incident as { damages: { itemType: string; amount: number }[] };\n  let payout = 0;\n  for (const damage of typedIncident.damages) {\n    payout += damage.amount - DEDUCTIBLE;\n  }\n  payout = Math.min(payout, policy.remainingCap);\n  return { payout: Math.floor(payout), remainingCap: policy.remainingCap - payout };\n};\n\nexport const processScenario = (input: ScenarioInput): { results: StepResult[] } => {\n  const results: StepResult[] = [];\n  const policies: (Policy | undefined)[] = [];\n  let quoteCount = 0;\n  for (const step of input.steps) {\n    const quoteStep = step as QuoteStep;\n    const claimStep = step as ClaimStep;\n    if (quoteStep.op === \"quote\") {\n      const isFirstQuote = quoteCount === 0;\n      results.push({\n        premium: calculateQuotePremium(quoteStep.items, input.customer, isFirstQuote),\n      });\n      const insuranceSum = quoteStep.items.reduce(\n        (sum, item) => sum + insuranceValueForItemType((item as Item).type),\n        0,\n      );\n      policies.push({ items: quoteStep.items, remainingCap: insuranceSum * CLAIM_CAP_MULTIPLIER });\n      quoteCount += 1;\n    } else if (claimStep.op === \"claim\") {\n      const policy = policies[claimStep.policy] as Policy;\n      const claimResult = processClaim(policy, claimStep.incident);\n      policy.remainingCap = claimResult.remainingCap;\n      results.push(claimResult);\n    }\n  }\n  return { results };\n};\n"}],"isError":false,"timestamp":1784925835120},{"role":"toolResult","toolCallId":"functions.read:1","toolName":"read","content":[{"type":"text","text":"import { describe, it, expect } from \"vitest\";\nimport { processScenario } from \"./claim-office.js\";\n\ndescribe(\"MHPCO Claim Office\", () => {\n  // Quote tests - ordered simple to complex\n  it(\"should quote an empty item list -- premium 5 G\", () => {\n    const input = {\n      customer: { yearsWithMHPCO: 0 },\n      steps: [{ op: \"quote\", items: [] }],\n    };\n    expect(processScenario(input)).toEqual({ results: [{ premium: 5 }] });\n  });\n  it(\"should quote a single sword -- premium 115 G\", () => {\n    const input = {\n      customer: { yearsWithMHPCO: 0 },\n      steps: [{ op: \"quote\", items: [{ type: \"sword\" }] }],\n    };\n    expect(processScenario(input)).toEqual({ results: [{ premium: 115 }] });\n  });\n  it(\"should quote a single amulet -- premium 71 G\", () => {\n    const input = {\n      customer: { yearsWithMHPCO: 0 },\n      steps: [{ op: \"quote\", items: [{ type: \"amulet\" }] }],\n    };\n    expect(processScenario(input)).toEqual({ results: [{ premium: 71 }] });\n  });\n  it(\"should quote a single rune -- premium 33 G\", () => {\n    const input = {\n      customer: { yearsWithMHPCO: 0 },\n      steps: [{ op: \"quote\", items: [{ type: \"rune\" }] }],\n    };\n    expect(processScenario(input)).toEqual({ results: [{ premium: 33 }] });\n  });\n  it(\"should quote two runes -- premium 60 G\", () => {\n    const input = {\n      customer: { yearsWithMHPCO: 0 },\n      steps: [{ op: \"quote\", items: [{ type: \"rune\" }, { type: \"rune\" }] }],\n    };\n    expect(processScenario(input)).toEqual({ results: [{ premium: 60 }] });\n  });\n  it(\"should quote three runes as a block -- premium 71 G\", () => {\n    const input = {\n      customer: { yearsWithMHPCO: 0 },\n      steps: [{ op: \"quote\", items: [{ type: \"rune\" }, { type: \"rune\" }, { type: \"rune\" }] }],\n    };\n    expect(processScenario(input)).toEqual({ results: [{ premium: 71 }] });\n  });\n  it(\"should quote four runes without block -- premium 115 G\", () => {\n    const input = {\n      customer: { yearsWithMHPCO: 0 },\n      steps: [\n        {\n          op: \"quote\",\n          items: [{ type: \"rune\" }, { type: \"rune\" }, { type: \"rune\" }, { type: \"rune\" }],\n        },\n      ],\n    };\n    expect(processScenario(input)).toEqual({ results: [{ premium: 115 }] });\n  });\n  it(\"should quote seven runes -- premium 198 G\", () => {\n    const input = {\n      customer: { yearsWithMHPCO: 0 },\n      steps: [\n        {\n          op: \"quote\",\n          items: [\n            { type: \"rune\" },\n            { type: \"rune\" },\n            { type: \"rune\" },\n            { type: \"rune\" },\n            { type: \"rune\" },\n            { type: \"rune\" },\n            { type: \"rune\" },\n          ],\n        },\n      ],\n    };\n    expect(processScenario(input)).toEqual({ results: [{ premium: 198 }] });\n  });\n  it(\"should quote 2 runes and 1 moonstone as different types -- premium 88 G\", () => {\n    const input = {\n      customer: { yearsWithMHPCO: 0 },\n      steps: [\n        {\n          op: \"quote\",\n          items: [{ type: \"rune\" }, { type: \"rune\" }, { type: \"moonstone\" }],\n        },\n      ],\n    };\n    expect(processScenario(input)).toEqual({ results: [{ premium: 88 }] });\n  });\n  it(\"should quote 3 runes and 3 moonstones as two separate blocks -- premium 137 G\", () => {\n    const input = {\n      customer: { yearsWithMHPCO: 0 },\n      steps: [\n        {\n          op: \"quote\",\n          items: [\n            { type: \"rune\" },\n            { type: \"rune\" },\n            { type: \"rune\" },\n            { type: \"moonstone\" },\n            { type: \"moonstone\" },\n            { type: \"moonstone\" },\n          ],\n        },\n      ],\n    };\n    expect(processScenario(input)).toEqual({ results: [{ premium: 137 }] });\n  });\n  it(\"should quote a cursed sword with 50% curse surcharge -- premium 165 G\", () => {\n    const input = {\n      customer: { yearsWithMHPCO: 0 },\n      steps: [{ op: \"quote\", items: [{ type: \"sword\", cursed: true }] }],\n    };\n    expect(processScenario(input)).toEqual({ results: [{ premium: 165 }] });\n  });\n  it(\"should quote a sword with enchantment 5 with 30% high-enchantment surcharge -- premium 145 G\", () => {\n    const input = {\n      customer: { yearsWithMHPCO: 0 },\n      steps: [{ op: \"quote\", items: [{ type: \"sword\", enchantment: 5 }] }],\n    };\n    expect(processScenario(input)).toEqual({ results: [{ premium: 145 }] });\n  });\n  it(\"should quote a cursed sword with enchantment 5 with both surcharges -- premium 195 G\", () => {\n    const input = {\n      customer: { yearsWithMHPCO: 0 },\n      steps: [{ op: \"quote\", items: [{ type: \"sword\", cursed: true, enchantment: 5 }] }],\n    };\n    expect(processScenario(input)).toEqual({ results: [{ premium: 195 }] });\n  });\n  it(\"should quote a sword for a long-standing customer (>=2 years) with 20% loyalty discount -- premium 95 G\", () => {\n    const input = {\n      customer: { yearsWithMHPCO: 2 },\n      steps: [{ op: \"quote\", items: [{ type: \"sword\" }] }],\n    };\n    expect(processScenario(input)).toEqual({ results: [{ premium: 95 }] });\n  });\n  it(\"should quote a sword as first insurance with 10% surcharge -- premium 115 G\", () => {\n    const input = {\n      customer: { yearsWithMHPCO: 0 },\n      steps: [{ op: \"quote\", items: [{ type: \"sword\" }] }],\n    };\n    expect(processScenario(input)).toEqual({ results: [{ premium: 115 }] });\n  });\n  it(\"should quote a second contract with 15% follow-up discount -- premium 100 G\", () => {\n    const