s*6\n= 44*1 + 61*1 + 24*2 + 12*4 + 7*5 + 2*6\n= 44 + 61 + 48 + 48 + 35 + 12\n= 248\n\nBefore: 260. Difference: -12.\n\nSo mass reduces from 260 to 248. Good.\n\nBut wait, I should verify these counts are consistent. The big changes are:\n- bindings -2 (removed typedItem, quoteStep, claimStep; added sum, damage, grossPayout, payout in processClaim; net -2)\n- invocations +3 (added reduce in processClaim; no other invocation changes)\n- conditionals -1 (removed else if)\n- assignments -2 (removed payout mutations)\n\nNet: -2*1 + 3*2 -1*4 -2*6 = -2 + 6 -4 -12 = -12. Correct.\n\nSo mass reduction of 12. Good.\n\nBut I want to double check if `else` counts as conditional. No, only `if` is a conditional. The `else` keyword is not counted. In original code, `else if (claimStep.op === \"claim\")` has two `if` keywords. In new code, just one `if`. So -1 conditional. Correct.\n\nNow, is the new code clearer? I think yes:\n- Uses TypeScript discriminated union instead of dual casts in processScenario.\n- Removes `unknown` and `as Item` casts by using proper types.\n- `processClaim` now uses functional reduce and reveals `grossPayout` intent.\n- `policies` is now `Policy[]` instead of `(Policy | undefined)[]`, removing the need for cast.\n\nThis is a good refactoring.\n\nLet me also consider if there are any runtime behavior changes. No, the types don't affect runtime. The processClaim refactor produces the same result. The else branch in processScenario only runs when op is not \"quote\", and since Step is QuoteStep | ClaimStep, it's \"claim\". Runtime behavior same.\n\nOne more thing: the `Item` type includes `material?: string` but it's not used in logic. That's fine.\n\nLet me verify TypeScript compiles with these changes. I'll write the file and run tests.\n\nActually, I need to be careful about the order of type declarations. TypeScript allows forward references for types. `QuoteStep` uses `Item` before it's declared. TypeScript handles this because types are hoisted. But to be safe and clear, I might declare `Item` before `QuoteStep`. Let me reorder:\n\n```typescript\ntype Item = { ... };\ntype Customer = { ... };\ntype QuoteStep = { op: \"quote\"; items: Item[] };\ntype ClaimStep = { op: \"claim\"; policy: number; incident: Incident };\ntype Step = QuoteStep | ClaimStep;\ntype Incident = { damages: Damage[] };\ntype Damage = { itemType: string; amount: number };\n```\n\nBut `Incident` uses `Damage` before `Damage` is declared. TypeScript handles forward references. But to avoid confusion, I'll declare Damage and Incident before ClaimStep:\n\n```typescript\ntype Item = { ... };\ntype Customer = { ... };\ntype Damage = { itemType: string; amount: number };\ntype Incident = { damages: Damage[] };\ntype QuoteStep = { op: \"quote\"; items: Item[] };\ntype ClaimStep = { op: \"claim\"; policy: number; incident: Incident };\ntype Step = QuoteStep | ClaimStep;\n```\n\nThis is clearer.\n\nAlso, `ScenarioInput` uses `Step`, so declare Step before ScenarioInput.\n\nLet me write the file.","thinkingSignature":"reasoning_content"},{"type":"toolCall","id":"functions.write:4","name":"write","arguments":{"path":"/home/experimenter/experiments/runs/2026-07-24_20-30-02_claim-office-example-mapping_v6.2-with-why-cleaned-pi_kimi-k2-7-no-thinking/src/claim-office.ts","content":"const PROCESSING_FEE = 5;\nconst FIRST_INSURANCE_SURCHARGE_RATE = 0.1;\nconst CURSE_SURCHARGE_RATE = 0.5;\n\nconst COMPONENT_TYPES = [\"rune\", \"moonstone\"];\nconst COMPONENT_BLOCK_SIZE = 3;\nconst COMPONENT_BLOCK_PREMIUM = 60;\nconst COMPONENT_UNIT_PREMIUM = 25;\n\ntype QuoteResult = { premium: number };\ntype ClaimResult = { payout: number; remainingCap: number };\ntype StepResult = QuoteResult | ClaimResult;\ntype Item = { type: string; cursed?: boolean; enchantment?: number; material?: string };\ntype Customer = { yearsWithMHPCO: number };\ntype Damage = { itemType: string; amount: number };\ntype Incident = { damages: Damage[] };\ntype QuoteStep = { op: \"quote\"; items: Item[] };\ntype ClaimStep = { op: \"claim\"; policy: number; incident: Incident };\ntype Step = QuoteStep | ClaimStep;\ntype Policy = { items: Item[]; remainingCap: number };\n\nconst basePremiumForItemType = (type: string): number => (type === \"amulet\" ? 60 : 100);\n\nconst insuranceValueForItemType = (type: string): number => {\n  if (type === \"sword\") return 1000;\n  if (type === \"amulet\") return 600;\n  if (type === \"staff\") return 800;\n  if (type === \"potion\") return 400;\n  if (type === \"rune\" || type === \"moonstone\") return 250;\n  return 0;\n};\n\nconst basePremiumForItem = (item: Item): number => basePremiumForItemType(item.type);\n\nconst HIGH_ENCHANTMENT_THRESHOLD = 5;\nconst HIGH_ENCHANTMENT_SURCHARGE_RATE = 0.3;\nconst LOYALTY_DISCOUNT_RATE = 0.2;\nconst LOYALTY_YEARS_THRESHOLD = 2;\nconst FOLLOW_UP_DISCOUNT_RATE = 0.15;\n\nconst surchargesForItem = (item: Item): number => {\n  const basePremium = basePremiumForItem(item);\n  const curseSurcharge = item.cursed ? basePremium * CURSE_SURCHARGE_RATE : 0;\n  const enchantmentSurcharge =\n    (item.enchantment ?? 0) >= HIGH_ENCHANTMENT_THRESHOLD\n      ? basePremium * HIGH_ENCHANTMENT_SURCHARGE_RATE\n      : 0;\n  return curseSurcharge + enchantmentSurcharge;\n};\n\nconst componentPremiumFor = (count: number): number =>\n  count === COMPONENT_BLOCK_SIZE ? COMPONENT_BLOCK_PREMIUM : count * COMPONENT_UNIT_PREMIUM;\n\nconst calculateFinalPremium = (\n  policyBase: number,\n  itemSurcharges: number,\n  yearsWithMHPCO: number,\n  isFirstQuote: boolean,\n): number => {\n  const loyaltyDiscount =\n    yearsWithMHPCO >= LOYALTY_YEARS_THRESHOLD ? LOYALTY_DISCOUNT_RATE : 0;\n  const followUpDiscount = isFirstQuote ? 0 : FOLLOW_UP_DISCOUNT_RATE;\n  const policyMultiplier =\n    1 + FIRST_INSURANCE_SURCHARGE_RATE - loyaltyDiscount - followUpDiscount;\n  const beforeFee = policyBase * policyMultiplier + itemSurcharges;\n  const roundedToNearestCent = Math.round(beforeFee * 100) / 100;\n  return Math.ceil(roundedToNearestCent + PROCESSING_FEE);\n};\n\nconst standardItemTotals = (items: Item[]): { base: number; surcharges: number } =>\n  items\n    .filter((item) => !COMPONENT_TYPES.includes(item.type))\n    .reduce(\n      (totals, item) => ({\n        base: totals.base + basePremiumForItem(item),\n        surcharges: totals.surcharges + surchargesForItem(item),\n      }),\n      { base: 0, surcharges: 0 },\n    );\n\nconst calculateQuotePremium = (\n  items: Item[],\n  customer: Customer,\n  isFirstQuote: boolean,\n): number => {\n  const { base: standardBase, surcharges: itemSurcharges } = standardItemTotals(items);\n  const componentBase = COMPONENT_TYPES.reduce((sum, type) => {\n    const count = items.filter((item) => item.type === type).length;\n    return sum + componentPremiumFor(count);\n  }, 0);\n  const policyBase = standardBase + componentBase;\n  return calculateFinalPremium(policyBase, itemSurcharges, customer.yearsWithMHPCO, isFirstQuote);\n};\n\ntype ScenarioInput = { customer: Customer; steps: Step[] };\n\nconst DEDUCTIBLE = 100;\nconst CLAIM_CAP_MULTIPLIER = 2;\n\nconst processClaim = (policy: Policy, incident: Incident): ClaimResult => {\n  const grossPayout = incident.damages.reduce(\n    (sum, damage) => sum + damage.amount - DEDUCTIBLE,\n    0,\n  );\n  const payout = Math.min(grossPayout, policy.remainingCap);\n  return { payout: Math.floor(payout), remainingCap: policy.remainingCap - payout };\n};\n\nexport const processScenario = (input: ScenarioInput): { results: StepResult[] } => {\n  const results: StepResult[] = [];\n  const policies: Policy[] = [];\n  let quoteCount = 0;\n  for (const step of input.steps) {\n    if (step.op === \"quote\") {\n      const isFirstQuote = quoteCount === 0;\n      results.push({\n        premium: calculateQuotePremium(step.items, input.customer, isFirstQuote),\n      });\n      const insuranceSum = step.items.reduce(\n        (sum, item) => sum + insuranceValueForItemType(item.type),\n        0,\n      );\n      policies.push({ items: step.items, remainingCap: insuranceSum * CLAIM_CAP_MULTIPLIER });\n      quoteCount += 1;\n    } else {\n      const policy = policies[step.policy];\n      const claimResult = processClaim(policy, step.incident);\n      policy.remainingCap = claimResult.remainingCap;\n      results.push(claimResult);\n    }\n  }\n  return { results };\n};\n"}}],"api":"openai-completions","provider":"requesty","model":"tensorx/kimi-k2.7-code","usage":{"input":9223,"output":11253,"cacheRead":12992,"cacheWrite":0,"reasoning":9718,"totalTokens":33468,"cost":{"input":0,"output":0,"cacheRead":0,"cacheWrite":0,"total":0}},"stopReason":"toolUse","timestamp":1784925904122,"responseId":"rqsty-cmpl-8f403029-a29a-4ea6-99a1-4a88a9dc7ef2","responseModel":"moonshotai/kimi-k2.7-code"},{"role":"toolResult","toolCallId":"functions.write:4","toolName":"write","content":[{"type":"text","text":"Successfully wrote 4898 bytes to /home/experimenter/experiments/runs/2026-07-24_20-30-02_claim-office-example-mapping_v6.2-with-why-cleaned-pi_kimi-k2-7-no-thinking/src/claim-office.ts"}],"isError":false,"timestamp":1784925967120},{"role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"thinking","thinking":"Now let me run tests and TypeScript check.","thinkingSignature":"reasoning_content"},{"type":"toolCall","id":"functions.bash:5","name":"bash","arguments":{"command":"cd /home/experimenter/experiments/runs/2026-07-24_20-30-02_claim-office-example-mapping_v6.2-with-why-cleaned-pi_kimi-k2-7-no-thinking && pnpm test","timeout":30}}],"api":"openai-completions","provider":"requesty","model":"tensorx/kimi-k2.7-code","usage":{"input":135,"output":85,"cacheRead":33408,"cacheWrite":0,"reasoning":11,"totalTokens":33628,"cost":{"input":0,"output":0,"cacheRead":0,"cacheWrite":0,"total":0}},"stopReason":"toolUse","timestamp":1784925967121,"responseId":"rqsty-cmpl-dbf1d647-fc2c-4aa7-a880-da3b44f56b78","responseModel":"moonshotai/kimi-k2.7-code"},{"role":"toolResult","toolCallId":"functions.bash:5","toolName":"bash"