oolResult","toolCallId":"functions.bash:134","toolName":"bash","content":[{"type":"text","text":"\n> tdd-experiment-run@ test /home/experimenter/experiments/runs/2026-07-24_20-30-02_claim-office-example-mapping_v6.2-with-why-cleaned-pi_kimi-k2-7-no-thinking\n> vitest run\n\n\n RUN  v1.6.1 /home/experimenter/experiments/runs/2026-07-24_20-30-02_claim-office-example-mapping_v6.2-with-why-cleaned-pi_kimi-k2-7-no-thinking\n\n ❯ src/claim-office.spec.ts  (33 tests | 1 failed | 11 skipped) 9ms\n   ❯ src/claim-office.spec.ts > MHPCO Claim Office > should apply 50% reimbursement for enchantment >= 8, then deductible -- payout 400 G\n     → expected { results: [ { premium: 145 }, …(1) ] } to deeply equal { results: [ { premium: 145 }, …(1) ] }\n\n⎯⎯⎯⎯⎯⎯⎯ Failed Tests 1 ⎯⎯⎯⎯⎯⎯⎯\n\n FAIL  src/claim-office.spec.ts > MHPCO Claim Office > should apply 50% reimbursement for enchantment >= 8, then deductible -- payout 400 G\nAssertionError: expected { results: [ { premium: 145 }, …(1) ] } to deeply equal { results: [ { premium: 145 }, …(1) ] }\n\n- Expected\n+ Received\n\n  Object {\n    \"results\": Array [\n      Object {\n        \"premium\": 145,\n      },\n      Object {\n-       \"payout\": 400,\n-       \"remainingCap\": 1600,\n+       \"payout\": 900,\n+       \"remainingCap\": 1100,\n      },\n    ],\n  }\n\n ❯ src/claim-office.spec.ts:242:36\n    240|       ],\n    241|     };\n    242|     expect(processScenario(input)).toEqual({\n       |                                    ^\n    243|       results: [{ premium: 145 }, { payout: 400, remainingCap: 1600 }],\n    244|     });\n\n⎯⎯⎯⎯⎯⎯⎯⎯⎯⎯⎯⎯⎯⎯⎯⎯⎯⎯⎯⎯⎯⎯⎯⎯[1/1]⎯\n\n Test Files  1 failed (1)\n      Tests  1 failed | 21 passed | 11 todo (33)\n   Start at  20:46:54\n   Duration  182ms (transform 37ms, setup 0ms, collect 37ms, tests 9ms, environment 0ms, prepare 49ms)\n\n ELIFECYCLE  Test failed. See above for more details.\n\n\nCommand exited with code 1"}],"details":{},"isError":true,"timestamp":1784926014864},{"role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"thinking","thinking":"Red complete. Green: add high enchantment claim rule.\n\nNeed to look up item properties for each damage. For damage itemType, find matching item in policy. Apply rules based on item.enchantment and item.material.","thinkingSignature":"reasoning_content"},{"type":"text","text":"Red Phase Complete:\n**Compilation Error Prediction**: None expected Correct\n**Runtime Prediction**: Expected payout 400, received 900 Correct\n**Result**: Test fails as expected with assertion error\n\nProceeding to Green phase.</think>## Green -- Test 22: high enchantment claim rule\n\n"},{"type":"toolCall","id":"functions.read:135","name":"read","arguments":{"path":"src/claim-office.ts"}}],"api":"openai-completions","provider":"requesty","model":"tensorx/kimi-k2.7-code","usage":{"input":660,"output":124,"cacheRead":73920,"cacheWrite":0,"reasoning":46,"totalTokens":74704,"cost":{"input":0,"output":0,"cacheRead":0,"cacheWrite":0,"total":0}},"stopReason":"toolUse","timestamp":1784926014867,"responseId":"rqsty-cmpl-ce6cf7d0-6cb9-4cf9-8627-7ffdc3f47470","responseModel":"moonshotai/kimi-k2.7-code"},{"role":"toolResult","toolCallId":"functions.read:135","toolName":"read","content":[{"type":"text","text":"const PROCESSING_FEE = 5;\nconst FIRST_INSURANCE_SURCHARGE_RATE = 0.1;\nconst CURSE_SURCHARGE_RATE = 0.5;\n\nconst COMPONENT_TYPES = [\"rune\", \"moonstone\"];\nconst COMPONENT_BLOCK_SIZE = 3;\nconst COMPONENT_BLOCK_PREMIUM = 60;\nconst COMPONENT_UNIT_PREMIUM = 25;\n\ntype QuoteResult = { premium: number };\ntype ClaimResult = { payout: number; remainingCap: number };\ntype StepResult = QuoteResult | ClaimResult;\ntype Item = { type: string; cursed?: boolean; enchantment?: number; material?: string };\ntype Customer = { yearsWithMHPCO: number };\ntype Damage = { itemType: string; amount: number };\ntype Incident = { damages: Damage[] };\ntype QuoteStep = { op: \"quote\"; items: Item[] };\ntype ClaimStep = { op: \"claim\"; policy: number; incident: Incident };\ntype Step = QuoteStep | ClaimStep;\ntype Policy = { items: Item[]; remainingCap: number };\n\nconst basePremiumForItemType = (type: string): number => (type === \"amulet\" ? 60 : 100);\n\nconst insuranceValueForItemType = (type: string): number => {\n  if (type === \"sword\") return 1000;\n  if (type === \"amulet\") return 600;\n  if (type === \"staff\") return 800;\n  if (type === \"potion\") return 400;\n  if (type === \"rune\" || type === \"moonstone\") return 250;\n  return 0;\n};\n\nconst basePremiumForItem = (item: Item): number => basePremiumForItemType(item.type);\n\nconst HIGH_ENCHANTMENT_THRESHOLD = 5;\nconst HIGH_ENCHANTMENT_SURCHARGE_RATE = 0.3;\nconst LOYALTY_DISCOUNT_RATE = 0.2;\nconst LOYALTY_YEARS_THRESHOLD = 2;\nconst FOLLOW_UP_DISCOUNT_RATE = 0.15;\n\nconst surchargesForItem = (item: Item): number => {\n  const basePremium = basePremiumForItem(item);\n  const curseSurcharge = item.cursed ? basePremium * CURSE_SURCHARGE_RATE : 0;\n  const enchantmentSurcharge =\n    (item.enchantment ?? 0) >= HIGH_ENCHANTMENT_THRESHOLD\n      ? basePremium * HIGH_ENCHANTMENT_SURCHARGE_RATE\n      : 0;\n  return curseSurcharge + enchantmentSurcharge;\n};\n\nconst componentPremiumFor = (count: number): number =>\n  count === COMPONENT_BLOCK_SIZE ? COMPONENT_BLOCK_PREMIUM : count * COMPONENT_UNIT_PREMIUM;\n\nconst calculateFinalPremium = (\n  policyBase: number,\n  itemSurcharges: number,\n  yearsWithMHPCO: number,\n  isFirstQuote: boolean,\n): number => {\n  const loyaltyDiscount =\n    yearsWithMHPCO >= LOYALTY_YEARS_THRESHOLD ? LOYALTY_DISCOUNT_RATE : 0;\n  const followUpDiscount = isFirstQuote ? 0 : FOLLOW_UP_DISCOUNT_RATE;\n  const policyMultiplier =\n    1 + FIRST_INSURANCE_SURCHARGE_RATE - loyaltyDiscount - followUpDiscount;\n  const beforeFee = policyBase * policyMultiplier + itemSurcharges;\n  const roundedToNearestCent = Math.round(beforeFee * 100) / 100;\n  return Math.ceil(roundedToNearestCent + PROCESSING_FEE);\n};\n\nconst standardItemTotals = (items: Item[]): { base: number; surcharges: number } =>\n  items\n    .filter((item) => !COMPONENT_TYPES.includes(item.type))\n    .reduce(\n      (totals, item) => ({\n        base: totals.base + basePremiumForItem(item),\n        surcharges: totals.surcharges + surchargesForItem(item),\n      }),\n      { base: 0, surcharges: 0 },\n    );\n\nconst calculateQuotePremium = (\n  items: Item[],\n  customer: Customer,\n  isFirstQuote: boolean,\n): number => {\n  const { base: standardBase, surcharges: itemSurcharges } = standardItemTotals(items);\n  const componentBase = COMPONENT_TYPES.reduce((sum, type) => {\n    const count = items.filter((item) => item.type === type).length;\n    return sum + componentPremiumFor(count);\n  }, 0);\n  const policyBase = standardBase + componentBase;\n  return calculateFinalPremium(policyBase, itemSurcharges, customer.yearsWithMHPCO, isFirstQuote);\n};\n\ntype ScenarioInput = { customer: Customer; steps: unknown[] };\n\nconst DEDUCTIBLE = 100;\nconst CLAIM_CAP_MULTIPLIER = 2;\n\nconst processClaim = (policy: Policy, incident: Incident): ClaimResult => {\n  const grossPayout = incident.damages.reduce(\n    (sum, damage) => sum + damage.amount - DEDUCTIBLE,\n    0,\n  );\n  const payout = Math.min(grossPayout, policy.remainingCap);\n  return { payout: Math.floor(payout), remainingCap: policy.remainingCap - payout };\n};\n\nexport const processScenario = (input: ScenarioInput): { results: StepResult[] } => {\n  const results: StepResult[] = [];\n  const policies: Policy[] = [];\n  let quoteCount = 0;\n  for (const step of input.steps) {\n    const typedStep = step as Step;\n    if (typedStep.op === \"quote\") {\n      const isFirstQuote = quoteCount === 0;\n      results.push({\n        premium: calculateQuotePremium(typedStep.items, input.customer, isFirstQuote),\n      });\n      const insuranceSum = typedStep.items.reduce(\n        (sum, item) => sum + insuranceValueForItemType(item.type),\n        0,\n      );\n      policies.push({\n        items: typedStep.items,\n        remainingCap: insuranceSum * CLAIM_CAP_MULTIPLIER,\n      });\n      quoteCount += 1;\n    } else {\n      const policy = policies[typedStep.policy];\n      const claimResult = processClaim(policy, typedStep.incident);\n      policy.remainingCap = claimResult.remainingCap;\n      results.push(claimResult);\n    }\n  }\n  return { results };\n};\n"}],"isError":false,"timestamp":1784926016595},{"role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"thinking","thinking":"I need to modify processClaim to look up item properties. For each damage:\n- Find item in policy with matching type\n- If item.enchantment >= 8, reimbursement = 50% of damage\n- Else if item.material === \"dragon\", reimbursement = 100%\n- Else reimbursement = 100%\n- Then subtract deductible\n\nBut what if multiple items of same type? Need to match damages to items. For now, just find first matching item. Later tests will require proper validation.\n\nFor minimal: find item by type, apply rate.","thinkingSignature":"reasoning_content"},{"type":"toolCall","id":"functions.edit:136","name":"edit","arguments":{"path":"src/claim-office.ts","edits":[{"oldText":"const DEDUCTIBLE = 100;\nconst CLAIM_CAP_MULTIPLIER = 2;","newText":"const DEDUCTIBLE = 100;\nconst CLAIM_CAP_MULTIPLIER = 2;\nconst HIGH_ENCHANTMENT_CLAIM_THRESHOLD = 8;\nconst HIGH_ENCHANTMENT_REIMBURSEMENT_RATE = 0.5;"},{"oldText":"const processClaim = (policy: Policy, incident: Incident): ClaimResult => {\n  const grossPayout = incident.damages.reduce(\n    (sum, damage) => sum + damage.amount - DEDUCTIBLE,\n    0,\n  );\n  const payout = Math.min(grossPayout, policy.remainingCap);\n  return { payout: Math.floor(payout), remainingCap: policy.remainingCap - payout };\n};","newText":"const reimbursementRateFor = (item: Item): number => {\n  if ((item.enchantment ?? 0) >= HIGH_ENCHANTMENT_CLAIM_THRESHOLD)\n    return HIGH_ENCHANTMENT_REIMBURSEMENT_RATE;\n  return 1;\n};\n\nconst processClaim = (policy: Policy, incident: In