ssClaim`, `reimbursementRateFor`, etc. all clearly describe their responsibilities.\n- No renaming required — names already reveal intent.\n\n### Changes Made\n\n1. **Extracted `policyMultiplierFor`** from `calculateFinalPremium`\n   - Reveals the intent of the policy-wide modifier calculation (first-insurance surcharge, loyalty discount, follow-up discount).\n   - Keeps `calculateFinalPremium` focused on fee/rounding.\n\n2. **Extracted `damagePayoutFor`** from `processClaim`\n   - Isolates per-damage reimbursement logic: find item → apply rate → subtract deductible.\n   - Makes `processClaim` read as \"sum damage payouts, then cap\".\n\n3. **Extracted `componentPremiumForItems`** from `calculateQuotePremium`\n   - Mirrors the existing `standardItemTotals` helper.\n   - Makes `calculateQuotePremium` express the quote structure at a glance.\n\n4. **Replaced if-chain with `INSURANCE_VALUES` lookup table**\n   - `insuranceValueForItemType` now looks up values instead of chaining 5 `if`s.\n   - Easier to extend and eliminates duplication of `===` checks.\n\n### APP Mass Calculation\n\n| Function | Before | After | Δ |\n|---|---:|---:|---:|\n| `calculateFinalPremium` + `policyMultiplierFor` | 44 | 48 | +4 |\n| `processClaim` + `damagePayoutFor` | 40 | 43 | +3 |\n| `calculateQuotePremium` + `componentPremiumForItems` | 38 | 39 | +1 |\n| `insuranceValueForItemType` + `INSURANCE_VALUES` | 45 | 13 | **-32** |\n| **Total changed functions** | **167** | **143** | **-24** |\n\nThe three extractions add small local mass (acceptable per Rule 2 — clarity over mass), while the lookup-table replacement removes a large block of conditionals and literals, yielding a net mass reduction.\n\n### Verification\n- `pnpm test`: **22 passing, 11 todo** ✅\n- `npx tsc --noEmit`: **no type errors** ✅\n\nTests remain green and behavior is preserved."}],"details":{"mode":"single","agentScope":"both","projectAgentsDir":"/home/experimenter/experiments/runs/2026-07-24_20-30-02_claim-office-example-ma