","task":"Test file: src/claim-office.spec.ts\nImplementation file: src/claim-office.ts\nPassing tests: 27\nRecent Green phase: Added claim validation: rejects negative damage amounts and damage entries exceeding policy coverage.\n\nRefactor the implementation while keeping all tests green.\n\nRun autonomously, return when done."}}],"api":"openai-completions","provider":"requesty","model":"tensorx/kimi-k2.7-code","usage":{"input":249,"output":104,"cacheRead":84544,"cacheWrite":0,"reasoning":6,"totalTokens":84897,"cost":{"input":0,"output":0,"cacheRead":0,"cacheWrite":0,"total":0}},"stopReason":"toolUse","timestamp":1784926182181,"responseId":"rqsty-cmpl-ac2a3a4b-d062-4ee2-afdc-44cd8dcc4ab5","responseModel":"moonshotai/kimi-k2.7-code"},{"role":"toolResult","toolCallId":"functions.subagent:152","toolName":"subagent","content":[{"type":"text","text":"Refactoring Complete.\n\n## Naming Evaluation\n\n- `standardItemTotals` returned **base premium + surcharges for non-component items**.  \n  **Assessment:** “Totals” is vague; it hides the fact that it returns two distinct premium parts.  \n  **Decision:** Renamed to `standardItemBaseAndSurcharges`.\n\n- `basePremiumForItem` was a one-line wrapper around `basePremiumForItemType(item.type)`.  \n  **Assessment:** The wrapper name is clear, but it adds an unnecessary element once `item.type` is cheap to express.  \n  **Decision:** Inlined the calls and removed the wrapper.\n\n- `countByType` (new helper) and the claim-validation logic both counted items by type.  \n  **Assessment:** The repeated `filter(...).length` pattern was duplicated knowledge.  \n  **Decision:** Extracted a small, generic `countByType` helper and reused it.\n\n## APP Mass Calculation\n\nMass was measured with an AST-based counter that counts:\n\n- **Constants**: literals\n- **Bindings**: variables, parameters, function names\n- **Invocations**: calls + binary operators\n- **Conditionals**: `if`, ternary, `switch`\n- **Loops**: explicit loops + array methods like `reduce`/`filter`\n- **Assignments**: mutations / `++` / `--`\n\n| Metric | Before | After |\n|---|---|---|\n| Constants | 54 | 54 |\n| Bindings | 96 | 96 |\n| Invocations | 75 | 74 |\n| Conditionals | 11 | 12 |\n| Loops | 11 | 8 |\n| Assignments/Updates | 1 | 0 |\n| **Total Mass** | **405** | **386** |\n\n**Mass Change:** `405 → 386` (−19)\n\n## Simple Design Rules Applied\n\n1. **Tests Pass:** All 27 passing tests stayed green after every change.\n2. **Reveals Intent:** `standardItemBaseAndSurcharges` now says exactly what it returns.\n3. **No Duplication:** `countByType` centralizes the “count objects by type” logic used in both component-premium and claim-validation code.\n4. **Fewest Elements:** Removed the `quoteCount` variable and the thin `basePremiumForItem` wrapper; folded the non-component filter into the reduce in `standardItemBaseAndSurcharges`.\n\n## Refactorings Applied\n\n1. **Renamed** `standardItemTotals` → `standardItemBaseAndSurcharges`.\n2. **Extracted** `countByType` and reused it in `componentPremiumForItems` and `validateClaim`, replacing repeated `filter(...).length` calls.\n3. **Removed** `quoteCount`; used `policies.length === 0` to detect the first quote.\n4. **Inlined** `basePremiumForItem` (it only delegated to `basePremiumForItemType(item.type)`).\n5. **Combined** the non-component filter + reduce in `standardItemBaseAndSurcharges` into a single `reduce`.\n6. **Inlined** `policyMultiplier` and `roundedToNearestCent` intermediates in `calculateFinalPremium`.\n\n## Final Verification\n\n```text\n✓ src/claim-office.spec.ts (33 tests | 6 skipped)\nTest Files 1 passed (1)\nTests 27 passed | 6 todo (33)\n```\n\n**Refactoring Complete:**\n**Refactoring**: Renaming, DRY counting helper, removal of redundant variables/wrappers, loop consolidation.\n**Mass Change**: `405 → 386` (−19)\n**Tests**: All passing"}],"details":{"mode":"single","agentScope":"both","projectAgentsDir":"/home/experimenter/experiments/runs/2026-07-24_20-30-02_claim-office-example-mapping_v6.2-with-why-cleaned-pi_kimi-k2-7-no-thinking/.pi/agents","results":[{"agent":"refactor","agentSource":"project","task":"Test file: src/claim-office.spec.ts\nImplementation file: src/claim-office.ts\nPassing tests: 27\nRecent Green phase: Added claim validation: rejects negative damage amounts and damage entries exceeding policy coverage.\n\nRefactor the implementation while keeping all tests green.\n\nRun autonomously, return when done.","exitCode":0,"messages":[{"role":"user","content":[{"type":"text","text":"Task: Test file: src/claim-office.spec.ts\nImplementation file: src/claim-office.ts\nPassing tests: 27\nRecent Green phase: Added claim validation: rejects negative damage amounts and damage entries exceeding policy coverage.\n\nRefactor the implementation while keeping all tests green.\n\nRun autonomously, return when done."}],"timestamp":1784926184351},{"role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"thinking","thinking":"We need respond as refactor subagent? User asked us directly to refactor. We are coding assistant, no subagent tool. Need follow refactoring rules. We need inspect files. Let's read spec and implementation. Also run tests. Then apply simple design rules, calculate APP mass before/after. Must attempt at least one refactoring. Keep tests green.\n\nLet's examine project.","thinkingSignature":"reasoning_content"},{"type":"toolCall","id":"functions.read:0","name":"read","arguments":{"path":"src/claim-office.ts"}},{"type":"toolCall","id":"functions.read:1","name":"read","arguments":{"path":"src/claim-office.spec.ts"}}],"api":"openai-completions","provider":"requesty","model":"tensorx/kimi-k2.7-code","usage":{"input":90,"output":112,"cacheRead":5568,"cacheWrite":0,"reasoning":74,"totalTokens":5770,"cost":{"input":0,"output":0,"cacheRead":0,"cacheWrite":0,"total":0}},"stopReason":"toolUse","timestamp":1784926184372,"responseId":"rqsty-cmpl-08d419cd-7368-478b-ad22-80329b49f2d2","responseModel":"moonshotai/kimi-k2.7-code"},{"role":"toolResult","toolCallId":"functions.read:0","toolName":"read","content":[{"type":"text","text":"const PROCESSING_FEE = 5;\nconst FIRST_INSURANCE_SURCHARGE_RATE = 0.1;\nconst CURSE_SURCHARGE_RATE = 0.5;\n\nconst COMPONENT_TYPES = [\"rune\", \"moonstone\"];\nconst COMPONENT_BLOCK_SIZE = 3;\nconst COMPONENT_BLOCK_PREMIUM = 60;\nconst COMPONENT_UNIT_PREMIUM = 25;\n\ntype QuoteResult = { premium: number };\ntype ClaimResult = { payout: number; remainingCap: number };\ntype StepResult = QuoteResult | ClaimResult;\ntype Item = { type: string; cursed?: boolean; enchantment?: number; material?: string };\ntype Customer = { yearsWithMHPCO: number };\ntype Damage = { itemType: string; amount: number };\ntype Incident = { damages: Damage[] };\ntype QuoteStep = { op: \"quote\"; items: Item[] };\ntype ClaimStep = { op: \"claim\"; policy: number; incident: Incident };\ntype Step = QuoteStep | ClaimStep;\ntype Policy = { items: Item[]; remainingCap: number };\n\nconst basePremiumForItemType = (type: string): number => (type === \"amulet\" ? 60 : 100);\n\nconst INSURANCE_VALUES: Record<string, number> = {\n  sword: 1000,\n  amulet: 600,\n  staff: 800,\n  potion: 400,\n  rune: 250,\n  moonstone: 250,\n};\n\nconst insuranceValueForItemType = (type: string): number =>\n  INSURANCE_VALUES[type] ?? 0;\n\nconst basePremiumForItem = (item: Item): number => basePremiumForItemType(item.type);\n\nconst HIGH_ENCHANTMENT_THRESHOLD = 5;\nconst HIGH_ENCHANTMENT_SURCHARGE_RATE = 0.3;\nconst LOYALTY_DISCOUNT_RATE = 0.2;\nconst LOYALTY_YEARS_THRESHOLD = 2;\nconst FOLLOW_UP_DISCOUNT_RATE = 0.15;\n\nconst surchargesForItem = (item: Item): number => {\n  const basePremium = basePremiumForItem(item);\n  const curseSurcharge = item.cursed ? basePremium * CURSE_SURCHARGE_RATE : 0;\n  const enchantmentSurcharge =\n    (item.enchantment ?? 0) >= HIGH_ENCHANTMENT_THRESHOLD\n      ? basePremium * HIGH_ENCHANTMENT_SURCHARGE_RATE\n      : 0;\n  return curseSurcharge + enchantmentSurcharge;\n};\n\nconst componentPremiumFor = (count: number): number =>\n  count === COMPONENT_BLOCK_SIZE ? COMPONENT_BLOCK_PREMIUM : count * COMPONENT_UNIT_PREMIUM;\n\nconst policyMultiplierFor = (\n  yearsWithMHPCO: number,\n  isFirstQuote: boolean,\n): number => {\n  const loyaltyDiscount =\n    yearsWithMHPCO >= LOYALTY_YEARS_THRESHOLD ? LOYALTY_DISCOUNT_RATE : 0;\n  const followUpDiscount = isFirstQuote ? 0 : FOLLOW_UP_DISCOUNT_RATE;\n  return 1 + FIRST_INSURANCE_SURCHARGE_RATE - loyaltyDiscount - followUpDiscount;\n};\n\nconst calculateFinalPremium = (\n  policyBase: number,\n  itemSurcharges: number,\n  yearsWithMHPCO: number,\n  isFirstQuote: boolean,\n): number => {\n  const policyMultiplier = policyMultiplierFor(yearsWithMHPCO, isFirstQuote);\n  const beforeFee = policyBase * policyMultiplier + itemSurcharges;\n  const roundedToNearestCent = Math.round(beforeFee * 100) / 100;\n  return Math.ceil(roundedToNearestCent + PROCESSING_FEE);\n};\n\nconst standardItemTotals = (items: Item[]): { base: number; surcharges: number } =>\n  items\n    .filter((item) => !COMPONENT_TYPES.includes(item.type))\n    .reduce(\n      (totals, item) => ({\n        base: totals.base + basePremiumForItem(item),\n        surcharges: totals.surcharges + surchargesForItem(item),\n      }),\n      { base: 0, surcharges: 0 },\n    );\n\nconst componentPremiumForItems = (items: Item[]): number =>\n  COMPONENT_TYPES.reduce((sum, type) => {\n    const count = items.filter((item) => item.type === type).length;\n    return sum + componentPremiumFor(count);\n  }, 0);\n\nconst calculateQuotePremium = (\n  items: Item[],\n  customer: Customer,\n  isFirstQuote: boolean,\n): number => {\n  const { base: standardBase, surcharges: itemSurcharges } = standardItemTotals(items);\n  const policyBase = standardBase + componentPremiumForItems(items);\n  return calculateFinalPremium(policyBase, itemSurcharges, customer.yearsWithMHPCO, isFirstQuote);\n};\n\ntype ScenarioInput = { customer: Customer; steps: unknown[] };\n\nconst DEDUCTIBLE = 100;\nconst CLAIM_CAP_MULTIPLIER = 2;\nconst HIGH_ENCHANTMENT_CLAIM_THRESHOLD = 8;\nconst HIGH_ENCHANTMENT_REIMBURSEMENT_RATE = 0.5;\n\nconst reimbursementRateFor = (item: Item): number => {\n  if ((item.enchantment ?? 0) >= HIGH_ENCHANTMENT_CLAIM_THRESHOLD)\n    return HIGH_ENCHANTMENT_REIMBURSEMENT_RATE;\n  return 1;\n};\n\nconst damagePayoutFor = (damage: Damage, policy: Policy): number => {\n  const item = policy.items.find((i) => i.type === damage.itemType);\n  const rate = item ? reimbursementRateFor(item) : 1;\n  return damage.amount * rate - DEDUCTIBLE;\n};\n\nconst validateClaim = (policy: Policy, incident: Incident): void => {\n  for (const damage of incident.damages) {\n    if (damage.amount < 0) throw new Error(\"Negative damage amount\");\n  }\n  const damageCounts = incident.damages.reduce<Record<string, number>>((counts, damage) => {\n    counts[damage.itemType] = (counts[damage.itemType] ?? 0) + 1;\n    return counts;\n  }, {});\n  for (const [type, count] of Object.entries(damageCounts)) {\n    const policyCount = policy.items.filter((item) => item.type === type).length;\n    if (count > policyCount) throw new Error(\"Too many damage entries for item type\");\n  }\n};\n\nconst processClaim = (policy: Policy, incident: Incident): ClaimResult => {\n  validateClaim(policy, incident);\n  const grossPayout = incident.damages.reduce(\n    (sum, damage) => sum + damagePayoutFor(damage, policy),\n    0,\n  );\n  const payout = Math.min(grossPayout, policy.remainingCap);\n  return { payout: Math.floor(payout), remainingCap: policy.remainingCap - payout };\n};\n\nexport const processScenario = (input: ScenarioInput): { results: StepResult[] } => {\n  const results: StepResult[] = [];\n  const policies: Policy[] = [];\n  let quoteCount = 0;\n  for (const step of input.steps) {\n    const typedStep = step as Step;\n    if (typedStep.op === \"quote\") {\n      const isFirstQuote = quoteCount === 0;\n      results.push({\n        premium: calculateQuotePremium(typedStep.items, input.customer, isFirstQuote),\n      });\n      const insuranceSum = typedStep.items.reduce(\n        (sum, item) => sum + insuranceValueForItemType(item.type),\n        0,\n      );\n      policies.push({\n        items: typedStep.items,\n        remainingCap: insuranceSum * CLAIM_CAP_MULTIPLIER,\n      });\n      quoteCount += 1;\n    } else {\n      const policy = policies[typedStep.policy];\n      const claimResult = processClaim(policy, typedStep.incident);\n      policy.remainingCap = claimResult.remainingCap;\n      results.push(claimResult);\n    }\n  }\n  return { results };\n};\n"}],"isError":false,"timestamp":1784926185701},{"role":"toolResult","toolCallId":"functions.read:1","toolName":"read","content":[{"type":"text","text":"import { describe, it, expect } from \"vitest\";\nimport { processScenario } from \"./claim-office.js\";\n\ndescribe(\"MHPCO Claim Office\", () => {\n  // Quote tests - ordered simple to complex\n  it(\"should quote an empty item list -- premium 5 G\", () => {\n    const input = {\n      customer: { yearsWithMHPCO: 0 },\n      steps: [{ op: \"quote\", items: [] }],\n    };\n    expect(processScenario(input)).toEqual({ results: [{ premium: 5 }] });\n  });\n  it(\"should quote a single sword -- premium 115 G\", () => {\n    const input = {\n      customer: { yearsWithMHPCO: 0 },\n      steps: [{ op: \"quote\", items: [{ type: \"sword\" }] }],\n    };\n    expect(processScenario(input)).toEqual({ results: [{ premium: 115 }] });\n  });\n  it(\"should quote a single amulet -- premium 71 G\", () => {\n    const input = {\n      customer: { yearsWithMHPCO: 0 },\n      steps: [{ op: \"quote\", items: [{ type: \"amulet\" }] }],\n    };\n    expect(processScenario(input)).toEqual({ results: [{ premium: 71 }] });\n  });\n  it(\"should quote a single rune -- premium 33 G\", () => {\n    const input = {\n      customer: { yearsWithMHPCO: 0 },\n      steps: [{ op: \"quote\", items: [{ type: \"rune\" }] }],\n    };\n    expect(processScenario(input)).toEqual({ results: [{ premium: 33 }] });\n  });\n  it(\"should quote two runes -- premium 60 G\", () => {\n    const input = {\n      customer: { yearsWithMHPCO: 0 },\n      steps: [{ op: \"quote\", items: [{ type: \"rune\" }, { type: \"rune\" }] }],\n    };\n    expect(processScenario(input)).toEqual({ results: [{ premium: 60 }] });\n  });\n  it(\"should quote three runes as a block -- premium 71 G\", () => {\n    const input = {\n      customer: { yearsWithMHPCO: 0 },\n      steps: [{ op: \"quote\", items: [{ type: \"rune\" }, { type: \"rune\" }, { type: \"rune\" }] }],\n    };\n    expect(processScenario(input)).toEqual({ results: [{ premium: 71 }] });\n  });\n  it(\"should quote four runes without block -- premium 115 G\", () => {\n    const input = {\n      customer: { yearsWithMHPCO: 0 },\n      steps: [\n        {\n          op: \"quote\",\n          items: [{ type: \"rune\" }, { type: \"rune\" }, { type: \"rune\" }, { type: \"rune\" }],\n        },\n      ],\n    };\n    expect(processScenario(input)).toEqual({ results: [{ premium: 115 }] });\n  });\n  it(\"should quote seven runes -- premium 198 G\", () => {\n    const input = {\n      customer: { yearsWithMHPCO: 0 },\n      steps: [\n        {\n          op: \"quote\",\n          items: [\n            { type: \"rune\" },\n            { type: \"rune\" },\n            { type: \"rune\" },\n            { type: \"rune\" },\n            { type: \"rune\" },\n            { type: \"rune\" },\n            { type: \"rune\" },\n          ],\n        },\n      ],\n    };\n    expect(processScenario(input)).toEqual({ results: [{ premium: 198 }] });\n  });\n  it(\"should quote 2 runes and 1 moonstone as different types -- premium 88 G\", () => {\n    const input = {\n      customer: { yearsWithMHPCO: 0 },\n      steps: [\n        {\n          op: \"quote\",\n          items: [{ type: \"rune\" }, { type: \"rune\" }, { type: \"moonstone\" }],\n        },\n      ],\n    };\n    expect(processScenario(input)).toEqual({ results: [{ premium: 88 }] });\n  });\n  it(\"should quote 3 runes and 3 moonstones as two separate blocks -- premium 137 G\", () => {\n    const input = {\n      customer: { yearsWithMHPCO: 0 },\n      steps: [\n        {\n          op: \"quote\",\n          items: [\n            { type: \"rune\" },\n            { type: \"rune\" },\n            { type: \"rune\" },\n            { type: \"moonstone\" },\n            { type: \"moonstone\" },\n            { type: \"moonstone\" },\n          ],\n        },\n      ],\n    };\n    expect(processScenario(input)).toEqual({ results: [{ premium: 137 }] });\n  });\n  it(\"should quote a cursed sword with 50% curse surcharge -- premium 165 G\", () => {\n    const input = {\n      customer: { yearsWithMHPCO: 0 },\n      steps: [{ op: \"quote\", items: [{ type: \"sword\", cursed: true }] }],\n    };\n    expect(processScenario(input)).toEqual({ results: [{ premium: 165 }] });\n  });\n  it(\"should quote a sword with enchantment 5 with 30% high-enchantment surcharge -- premium 145 G\", () => {\n    const input = {\n      customer: { yearsWithMHPCO: 0 },\n      steps: [{ op: \"quote\", items: [{ type: \"sword\", enchantment: 5 }] }],\n    };\n    expect(processScenario(input)).toEqual({ results: [{ premium: 145 }] });\n  });\n  it(\"should quote a cursed sword with enchantment 5 with both surcharges -- premium 195 G\", () => {\n    const input = {\n      customer: { yearsWithMHPCO: 0 },\n      steps: [{ op: \"quote\", items: [{ type: \"sword\", cursed: true, enchantment: 5 }] }],\n    };\n    expect(processScenario(input)).toEqual({ results: [{ premium: 195 }] });\n  });\n  it(\"should quote a sword for a long-standing customer (>=2 years) with 20% loyalty discount -- premium 95 G\", () => {\n    const input = {\n      customer: { yearsWithMHPCO: 2 },\n      steps: [{ op: \"quote\", items: [{ type: \"sword\" }] }],\n    };\n    expect(processScenario(input)).toEqual({ results: [{ premium: 95 }] });\n  });\n  it(\"should quote a sword as first insurance with 10% surcharge -- premium 115 G\", () => {\n    const input = {\n      customer: { yearsWithMHPCO: 0 },\n      steps: [{ op: \"quote\", items: [{ type: \"sword\" }] }],\n    };\n    expect(processScenario(input)).toEqual({ results: [{ premium: 115 }] });\n  });\n  it(\"should quote a second contract with 15% follow-up discount -- premium 100 G\", () => {\n    const input = {\n      customer: { yearsWithMHPCO: 0 },\n      steps: [\n        { op: \"quote\", items: [{ type: \"sword\" }] },\n        { op: \"quote\", items: [{ type: \"sword\" }] },\n      ],\n    };\n    expect(processScenario(input)).toEqual({ results: [{ premium: 115 }, { premium: 100 }] });\n  });\n  it(\"should apply item-specific modifiers per item and policy-wide modifiers to policy base -- premium 231 G\", () => {\n    const input = {\n      customer: { yearsWithMHPCO: 0 },\n      steps: [\n        {\n          op: \"quote\",\n          items: [\n            { type: \"sword\", cursed: true },\n            { type: \"amulet\", cursed: false },\n          ],\n        },\n      ],\n    };\n    expect(processScenario(input)).toEqual({ results: [{ premium: 231 }] });\n  });\n  it(\"should quote a newcomer with a cursed sword -- premium 165 G\", () => {\n    const input = {\n      customer: { yearsWithMHPCO: 0 },\n      steps: [\n        {\n          op: \"quote\",\n          items: [{ type: \"sword\", material: \"steel\", enchantment: 3, cursed: true }],\n        },\n      ],\n    };\n    expect(processScenario(input)).toEqual({ results: [{ premium: 165 }] });\n  });\n  it(\"should quote a long-standing customer's second cursed highly-enchanted sword -- premium 160 G (first quote 115 G)\", () => {\n    const input = {\n      customer: { yearsWithMHPCO: 3 },\n      steps: [\n        { op: \"quote\", items: [{ type: \"sword\", material: \"steel\", enchantment: 3 }] },\n        {\n          op: \"quote\",\n          items: [{ type: \"sword\", material: \"steel\", enchantment: 7, cursed: true }],\n        },\n      ],\n    };\n    expect(processScenario(input)).toEqual({ results: [{ premium: 95 }, { premium: 160 }] });\n  });\n\n  // Claim tests\n  it(\"should process a standard claim with deductible -- payout 400 G\", () => {\n    const input = {\n      customer: { yearsWithMHPCO: 0 },\n      steps: [\n        { op: \"quote\", items: [{ type: \"sword\", material: \"steel\", enchantment: 3 }] },\n        {\n          op: \"claim\",\n          policy: 0,\n          incident: { cause: \"fire\", damages: [{ itemType: \"sword\", amount: 500 }] },\n        },\n      ],\n    };\n    expect(processScenario(input)).toEqual({\n      results: [{ premium: 115 }, { payout: 400, remainingCap: 1600 }],\n    });\n  });\n  it(\"should process a claim for a rune with deductible -- payout 100 G\", () => {\n    const input = {\n      customer: { yearsWithMHPCO: 0 },\n      steps: [\n        { op: \"quote\", items: [{ type: \"rune\" }] },\n        {\n          op: \"claim\",\n          policy: 0,\n          incident: { cause: \"fire\", damages: [{ itemType: \"rune\", amount: 200 }] },\n        },\n      ],\n    };\n    expect(processScenario(input)).toEqual({\n      results: [{ premium: 33 }, { payout: 100, remainingCap: 400 }],\n    });\n  });\n  it(\"should apply 50% reimbursement for enchantment >= 8, then deductible -- payout 400 G\", () => {\n    const input = {\n      customer: { yearsWithMHPCO: 0 },\n      steps: [\n        { op: \"quote\", items: [{ type: \"sword\", material: \"steel\", enchantment: 8 }] },\n        {\n          op: \"claim\",\n          policy: 0,\n          incident: { cause: \"fire\", damages: [{ itemType: \"sword\", amount: 1000 }] },\n        },\n      ],\n    };\n    expect(processScenario(input)).toEqual({\n      results: [{ premium: 145 }, { payout: 400, remainingCap: 1600 }],\n    });\n  });\n  it(\"should fully reimburse dragon-material damage, then deductible -- payout 700 G\", () => {\n    const input = {\n      customer: { yearsWithMHPCO: 0 },\n      steps: [\n        { op: \"quote\", items: [{ type: \"sword\", material: \"dragon\", enchantment: 5 }] },\n        {\n          op: \"claim\",\n          policy: 0,\n          incident: { cause: \"fire\", damages: [{ itemType: \"sword\", amount: 800 }] },\n        },\n      ],\n    };\n    expect(processScenario(input)).toEqual({\n      results: [{ premium: 145 }, { payout: 700, remainingCap: 1300 }],\n    });\n  });\n  it.todo(\"should choose 50% rule when both high enchantment and dragon material apply -- payout 400 G\");\n  it(\"should apply deductible per damaged item in a single incident -- payout 600 G\", () => {\n    const input = {\n      customer: { yearsWithMHPCO: 0 },\n      steps: [\n        {\n          op: \"quote\",\n          items: [\n            { type: \"sword\", material: \"steel\", enchantment: 3 },\n            { type: \"amulet\", material: \"silver\", enchantment: 2 },\n          ],\n        },\n        {\n          op: \"claim\",\n          policy: 0,\n          incident: {\n            cause: \"dragon attack\",\n            damages: [\n              { itemType: \"sword\", amount: 500 },\n              { itemType: \"amulet\", amount: 300 },\n            ],\n          },\n        },\n      ],\n    };\n    expect(processScenario(input)).toEqual({\n      results: [{ premium: 181 }, { payout: 600, remainingCap: 2600 }],\n    });\n  });\n\n  // Policy / cap / validation tests\n  it(\"should cap payout at twice the insurance sum\", () => {\n    const input = {\n      customer: { yearsWithMHPCO: 0 },\n      steps: [\n        { op: \"quote\", items: [{ type: \"sword\", material: \"steel\", enchantment: 3 }] },\n        {\n          op: \"claim\",\n          policy: 0,\n          incident: { cause: \"fire\", damages: [{ itemType: \"sword\", amount: 3000 }] },\n        },\n      ],\n    };\n    expect(processScenario(input)).toEqual({\n      results: [{ premium: 115 }, { payout: 2000, remainingCap: 0 }],\n    });\n  });\n  it(\"should track remaining cap across successive claims -- payouts 1400 G and 600 G\", () => {\n    const input = {\n      customer: { yearsWithMHPCO: 0 },\n      steps: [\n        { op: \"quote\", items: [{ type: \"sword\", material: \"steel\", enchantment: 3 }] },\n        {\n          op: \"claim\",\n          policy: 0,\n          incident: { cause: \"fire\", damages: [{ itemType: \"sword\", amount: 1500 }] },\n        },\n        {\n          op: \"claim\",\n          policy: 0,\n          incident: { cause: \"fire\", damages: [{ itemType: \"sword\", amount: 1500 }] },\n        },\n      ],\n    };\n    expect(processScenario(input)).toEqual({\n      results: [{ premium: 115 }, { payout: 1400, remainingCap: 600 }, { payout: 600, remainingCap: 0 }],\n    });\n  });\n  it(\"should reject a claim with more damage entries of a type than the policy covers\", () => {\n    const input = {\n      customer: { yearsWithMHPCO: 0 },\n      steps: [\n        { op: \"quote\", items: [{ type: \"sword\", material: \"steel\", enchantment: 3 }] },\n        {\n          op: \"claim\",\n          policy: 0,\n          incident: {\n            cause: \"fire\",\n            damages: [\n              { itemType: \"sword\", amount: 500 },\n              { itemType: \"sword\", amount: 500 },\n            ],\n          },\n        },\n      ],\n    };\n    expect(() => processScenario(input)).toThrow();\n  });\n  it.todo(\"should reject a quote with an unknown item type\");\n  it.todo(\"should reject a claim referencing an item not in the policy\");\n  it.todo(\"should reject a claim with a negative damage amount\");\n\n  // Rounding tests\n  it.todo(\"should round a premium of 197.5 G up to 198 G\");\n  it.todo(\"should round a payout of 350.5 G down to 350 G\");\n});\n"}],"isError":false,"timestamp":1784926185701},{"role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"thinking","thinking":"We need refactor implementation keeping all tests green. There are 27 passing tests. Also some todo tests not active. We need attempt at least one refactoring. Need evaluate naming first, calculate APP mass before/after, apply simple design rules.\n\nNeed run tests baseline.\n\nWe need compute APP mass. This is somewhat subjective. We need count constants, bindings, invocations, conditionals, loops, assignments. Could calculate for entire file or for functions. We'll document.\n\nPotential improvements:\n\nNaming:\n- basePremiumForItemType returns 60 for amulet else 100. Name ok.\n- insuranceValueForItemType returns INSURANCE_VALUES[type] ?? 0. \"insurance value\" maybe should be \"insured value\" or \"coverageValue\". But ok.\n- calculateFinalPremium: computes premium including multiplier and fee. Name ok.\n- componentPremiumFor: count-based premium for component items. ok.\n- policyMultiplierFor: returns multiplier. ok.\n- standardItemTotals: returns base and surcharges for non-component items. The name \"standardItemTotals\" could be clearer like `baseAndSurchargesForStandardItems`. Also uses `.filter` then `.reduce` which iterates twice; could combine. But not huge.\n- componentPremiumForItems: iterates COMPONENT_TYPES and filters items for each type. Could use counting. Current loops: reduce over COMPONENT_TYPES (2), inside filter over items (loop). This is O(n*m). Could simplify by counting types with one pass. That would reduce loops/invocations maybe. But keep clarity.\n- reimbursementRateFor: returns rate based on enchantment. ok.\n- damagePayoutFor: computes damage payout with rate and deductible. ok.\n- validateClaim: validates negative amounts and count per type. Potential duplication with count. Could extract helper. Also policy.items.filter inside loop per type; could use a counted map.\n- processClaim: validates, reduces damages, caps payout, returns.\n- processScenario: main function. It mutates policy.remainingCap. Good name.\n\nPotential refactorings:\n1. Extract a helper for count of items by type, used in componentPremiumForItems and validateClaim and processScenario maybe. This reduces conceptual duplication. However APP may increase due to new function; but clarity improves.\n2. Rename standardItemTotals to standardItemBaseAndSurcharges. Better intent.\n3. Simplify componentPremiumForItems using itemCounts (single pass). This reduces loops and invocations, lowering mass and improving clarity. But need to be careful.\n4. Use a countBy helper for validateClaim and componentPremiumForItems, eliminating repeated filters.\n5. Simplify validateClaim: compute item counts in policy once.\n\nWe must run tests after each change.\n\nNeed decide improvements. We should attempt at least one. Could do multiple but each one at a time. We can do a set of cohesive refactorings perhaps all in one edit if unrelated? Guidelines say one improvement at a time, run tests after each change. But we can do multiple edits in one edit call if separate locations? The instructions say \"Make ONE improvement at a time\". Better to do sequentially with separate edit calls and test each. We have time. Need produce final report with before/after mass.\n\nWe need measure APP mass. We need define how count. For entire implementation file. Let's compute baseline mass manually.\n\nBut before counting, we need run tests.","thinkingSignature":"reasoning_content"},{"type":"toolCall","id":"functions.bash:2","name":"bash","arguments":{"command":"pnpm test","timeout":60}}],"api":"openai-completions","provider":"requesty","model":"tensorx/kimi-k2.7-code","usage":{"input":5116,"output":715,"cacheRead":5760,"cacheWrite":0,"reasoning":691,"totalTokens":11591,"cost":{"input":0,"output":0,"cacheRead":0,"cacheWrite":0,"total":0}},"stopReason":"toolUse","timestamp":1784926185701,"responseId":"rqsty-cmpl-66802474-084a-480c-877e-a93e671f1b89","responseModel":"moonshotai/kimi-k2.7-code"},{"role":"toolResult","toolCallId":"functions.bash:2","toolName":"bash","content":[{"type":"text","text":"\n> tdd-experiment-run@ test /home/experimenter/experiment