ful.\n\nMaybe easiest: write a Python/Node script to count AST nodes:\n- constants: NumericLiteral, StringLiteral, BooleanLiteral, ArrayExpression maybe count as 1? We'll count Literal nodes only.\n- bindings: variable declarations + function params + function declarations.\n- invocations: CallExpression + BinaryExpression (each binary op) + UpdateExpression? Maybe UpdateExpression is assignment/invocation? In APP example `count++` is assignment, not invocation. We'll treat UpdateExpression as assignment.\n- conditionals: IfStatement + ConditionalExpression + SwitchStatement.\n- loops: ForStatement, ForInStatement, ForOfStatement, WhileStatement, DoWhileStatement, and array methods `reduce`, `forEach`, `map`, `filter`? The example says loops: Iteration (`for`, `forEach`, `map`). So CallExpression where callee is `reduce`, `forEach`, `map`, `filter`, `find`, `some`, `every` counts as loop. This adds complexity. We can count CallExpression if callee name is one of those. But we can just count `reduce`, `forEach`, `map`, `filter`. Also `Object.entries` not loop. `Array.from` not.\n- assignments: AssignmentExpression + UpdateExpression + VariableDeclarator? Variable declaration is binding, assignment is mutation. So `counts[damage.itemType] = ...` assignment. `x += 1` assignment. `quoteCount += 1` assignment. `count++` assignment.\n\nThis script can produce counts for the file or functions. But implementing function-level extraction maybe complex. We can parse whole file and count nodes. Good enough. We'll compare whole file mass before and after. That is objective.\n\nLet's write a Node script using @babel/parser? It may not be installed. TypeScript compiler API is available via `typescript` package? We have `tsc`. We can require typescript. Let's check.","thinkingSignature":"reasoning_content"},{"type":"toolCall","id":"functions.bash:6","name":"bash","arguments":{"command":"node -e \"console.log(require.resolve('typescript'))\"","timeout":30}}],"api":"openai-completions","provider":"requesty","model":"tensorx/kimi-k2.7-code","usage":{"input":3928,"output":1228,"cacheRead":14592,"cacheWrite":0,"reasoning":1195,"totalTokens":19748,"cost":{"input":0,"output":0,"cacheRead":0,"cacheWrite":0,"total":0}},"stopReason":"toolUse","timestamp":1784926208320,"responseId":"rqsty-cmpl-30178a94-0723-4c71-b46f-af1ebd878df7","responseModel":"moonshotai/kimi-k2.7-code"},{"role":"toolResult","toolCallId":"functions.bash:6","toolName":"bash","content":[{"type":"text","text":"/home/experimenter/experiments/runs/2026-07-24_20-30-02_claim-office-example-mapping_v6.2-with-why-cleaned-pi_kimi-k2-7-no-thinking/node_modules/.pnpm/typescript@5.9.3/node_modules/typescript/lib/typescript.js\n"}],"isError":false,"timestamp":1784926215777},{"role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"thinking","thinking":"We can use TypeScript. Let's write a script `mass.js` to parse TS and count. Need define visitor.\n\nBut maybe we don't need perfect AST; manual count for changed functions enough. However, we can use AST for whole file and compute before/after. Let's write script.\n\nImplementation details:\n- Parse source with ts.createSourceFile, ts.ScriptTarget.Latest, setParentNodes true.\n- Recursively visit nodes.\n- Count constants: NumericLiteral, StringLiteral, TrueKeyword, FalseKeyword. (RegexLiteral maybe none). BigInt none.\n- Count bindings: For each `VariableDeclaration` identifier, function parameters, function declaration name. Also maybe catch clause variable. Count each identifier binding. For destructuring, count each bound identifier. We'll use helper to collect binding identifiers.\n- Count invocations: BinaryExpression, CallExpression. Also maybe PostfixUnaryExpression? No, that's assignment/update. Prefix? assignment. OptionalCall? Call.\n- Count conditionals: IfStatement, ConditionalExpression, SwitchStatement, CaseClause? The guidelines say control flow `if`, `switch`, `?:`. We'll count IfStatement, ConditionalExpression, SwitchStatement. Maybe `CaseClause` not.\n- Count loops: ForStatement, ForInStatement, ForOfStatement, WhileStatement, DoWhileStatement. Also CallExpression where property name is one of [\"reduce\",\"forEach\",\"map\",\"filter\"]. Need to count even if method of array. For `numbers.reduce(...)`, count as loop. For `COMPONENT_TYPES.reduce(...)` count as loop. For `items.filter(...).reduce(...)` count both filter and reduce as loops. For `Object.entries(...).filter` not likely.\n- Count assignments: AssignmentExpression, PostfixUnaryExpression, PrefixUnaryExpression. Also `VariableDeclaration`? Not assignment. Binding.\n\nNeed ensure we don't double-count. A CallExpression is both invocation and maybe loop; both counted separately. A BinaryExpression invocation. An UpdateExpression assignment.\n\nPotential issue: Type annotations include identifiers but we won't count them. Type aliases not counted. Type references not counted.\n\nLet's test script on the current file.","thinkingSignature":"reasoning_content"},{"type":"toolCall","id":"functions.write:7","name":"write","arguments":{"path":"mass.js","content":"const ts = require(\"typescript\");\nconst fs = require(\"fs\");\n\nconst file = process.argv[2] || \"src/claim-office.ts\";\nconst source = fs.readFileSync(file, \"utf8\");\nconst srcFile = ts.createSourceFile(file, source, ts.ScriptTarget.Latest, true);\n\nconst loopMethods = new Set([\"reduce\", \"forEach\", \"map\", \"filter\"]);\n\nfunction collectBindings(node) {\n  const bindings = [];\n  function walk(n) {\n    if (ts.isIdentifier(n)) {\n      bindings.push(n);\n      return;\n    }\n    if (ts.isArrayBindingPattern(n) || ts.isObjectBindingPattern(n)) {\n      n.forEachChild(walk);\n    }\n  }\n  walk(node);\n  return bindings;\n}\n\nconst counts = {\n  constants: 0,\n  bindings: 0,\n  invocations: 0,\n  conditionals: 0,\n  loops: 0,\n  assignments: 0,\n};\n\nfunction visit(node) {\n  switch (node.kind) {\n    case ts.SyntaxKind.NumericLiteral:\n    case ts.SyntaxKind.StringLiteral:\n    case ts.SyntaxKind.TrueKeyword:\n    case ts.SyntaxKind.FalseKeyword:\n      counts.constants++;\n      break;\n    case ts.SyntaxKind.VariableDeclaration:\n      counts.bindings += collectBindings(node.name).length;\n      break;\n    case ts.SyntaxKind.Parameter:\n      counts.bindings += collectBindings(node.name).length;\n      break;\n    case ts.SyntaxKind.FunctionDeclaration:\n      if (node.name) counts.bindings += 1;\n      break;\n    case ts.SyntaxKind.ArrowFunction:\n      // arrow parameters already visited as Parameter nodes if parent is Parameter?\n      // Actually for arrow functions, parameters are Parameter nodes too.\n      break;\n    case ts.SyntaxKind.BinaryExpression:\n      counts.invocations++;\n      break;\n    case ts.SyntaxKind.CallExpression:\n    case ts.SyntaxKind.OptionalCallExpression:\n      counts.invocations++;\n      if (\n        ts.isPropertyAccessExpression(node.expression) &&\n        loopMethods.has(node.expression.name.text)\n      ) {\n        counts.loops++;\n      }\n      break;\n    case ts.SyntaxKind.IfStatement:\n    case ts.SyntaxKind.ConditionalExpression:\n    case ts.SyntaxKind.SwitchStatement:\n      counts.conditionals++;\n      break;\n    case ts.SyntaxKind.ForStatement:\n    case ts.SyntaxKind.ForInStatement:\n    case ts.SyntaxKind.ForOfStatement:\n    case ts.SyntaxKind.WhileStatement:\n    case ts.SyntaxKind.DoStatement:\n      counts.loops++;\n      break;\n    case ts.SyntaxKind.AssignmentExpression:\n      counts.assignments++;\n      break;\n    case ts.SyntaxKind.PostfixUnaryExpression:\n    case ts.SyntaxKind.PrefixUnaryExpression:\n      counts.assignments++;\n      break;\n  }\n  ts.forEachChild(node, visit);\n}\n\nvisit(srcFile);\n\nconst total =\n  counts.constants * 1 +\n  counts.bindings * 1 +\n  counts.invocations * 2 +\n  counts.conditionals * 4 +\n  counts.loops * 5 +\n  counts.assignments * 6;\n\nconsole.log(\"Component Counts:\");\nconsole.log(counts);\nconsole.log(\"Total Mass:\", tota