0 = 350.5. But damage must be integer, 901 is integer. So payout 350.5, floor = 350.\n\nBut wait, the spec example says \"a payout calculation that yields 350.5 G → final payout 350 G (rounded down)\". The damage amount could be 901. But the spec doesn't specify the scenario. I can use any.\n\nActually, I realize current code uses `Math.floor(payout)`. But payout could be negative. Need to ensure floor works as intended. For 350.5, floor = 350. Good.\n\nLet me create test: sword enchantment 8, damage 901. 50% = 450.5, -100 = 350.5, floor 350. Cap 2000. Remaining cap 1650.\n\nWait, the spec says \"intermediate amounts during a calculation are kept as fractions; only the final premium or payout is rounded\". So 450.5 - 100 = 350.5, final floor 350.\n\nActivate.","thinkingSignature":"reasoning_content"},{"type":"toolCall","id":"functions.edit:164","name":"edit","arguments":{"path":"src/claim-office.spec.ts","edits":[{"oldText":"  it.todo(\"should round a payout of 350.5 G down to 350 G\");","newText":"  it(\"should round a payout of 350.5 G down to 350 G\", () => {\n    const input = {\n      customer: { yearsWithMHPCO: 0 },\n      steps: [\n        { op: \"quote\", items: [{ type: \"sword\", material: \"steel\", enchantment: 8 }] },\n        {\n          op: \"claim\",\n          policy: 0,\n          incident: { cause: \"fire\", damages: [{ itemType: \"sword\", amount: 901 }] },\n        },\n      ],\n    };\n    expect(processScenario(input)).toEqual({\n      results: [{ premium: 145 }, { payout: 350, remainingCap: 1650 }],\n    });\n  });"}]}}],"api":"openai-completions","provider":"requesty","model":"tensorx/kimi-k2.7-code","usage":{"input":259,"output":670,"cacheRead":89152,"cacheWrite":0,"reasoning":434,"totalTokens":90081,"cost":{"input":0,"output":0,"cacheRead":0,"cacheWrite":0,"total":0}},"stopReason":"toolUse","timestamp":1784926446202,"responseId":"rqsty-cmpl-8f7fa230-3970-43cf-8335-d5cefa6f038a","responseModel":"moonshotai/kimi-k2.7-code"},{"role":"toolRes